// Macro expansion: the pass that rewrites the AST every other pass reads.
//
// Written in subset 1 (meta/SUBSET_1.md §4). Cycle 0.6.1.
//
// EXPANSION PRECEDES EVERYTHING — name resolution, type checking, every static
// analysis. What those passes see is the expanded program, which is what makes
// this pass different in kind from all of them: they READ the tree and report,
// and a defect in one produces a wrong diagnostic. **A defect here produces a
// well-formed AST that means something other than what was written**, and every
// pass after it then analyses that faithfully.
//
// IT RUNS TO A FIXED POINT, because a macro body may contain invocations
// (`MACRO_REFERENCE.md` §6). One pass is not enough: `#outer()` expands to
// `{ #inner(); f3 }`, and `#inner()` expands on the round after.
//
// AND THE LOOP IS BOUNDED, which is D-057's addition to what the corpus specified:
// `macro:m = () { #m(); };` iterates forever, so the prototype fails to terminate.
// That is unacceptable in a compiler under formal verification, where termination
// is itself a property to be established.
//
// TWO BOUNDS, NOT ONE, because they are different mistakes. A deeply nested single
// expansion is a program that is too complicated; two macros expanding into each
// other is a program that does not terminate. One budget would report them alike,
// and the fix for each is unrelated — the same argument that gave exhaustiveness
// three codes rather than one (D-120).
//
// EVERY INSTANTIATION IS A CLONE. Two invocations of one macro produce two
// separate subtrees, because they may substitute different arguments — sharing the
// body's nodes would make the second invocation rewrite the first.

mod:expand;
use "../source_location.npk".*;
use "../ast_kind.npk".*;
use "../ast.npk".*;
use "../intern.npk".*;
use "../diagnostics.npk".*;
use "../token_kind.npk".*;
use "../parse_type.npk".*;   // the type accessors: the walk enters types (DEF-170, 1.6.1e step 3)
use "../parse_expr.npk".*;
use "../parse_stmt.npk".*;
use "../parse_pick.npk".*;
use "../parse_decl.npk".*;
use "../parse_decorate.npk".*;
use "../builtins.npk".*;
use "./macro_codes.npk".*;
use "../ast_depth.npk".*;

// THE TWO BOUNDS, and they bound different things — see the header.
//
// `EXPAND_DEPTH` STOOD HERE AND NOTHING USED IT (found by 0.6.6's code audit, which
// asks a related question: every code has a test). It was declared at 32 while
// `CLONE_FUEL` at 512 did the work, so the compiler had a constant naming a bound
// it did not enforce and a bound whose name did not say what it was. A number
// nothing reads is worse than no number: it reads as a decision somebody made.
//
// One depth bound, named for what it does. 512 rather than 32 because it counts
// NODES rather than macro invocations, and an ordinary expression is several nodes
// deep before anybody has nested anything.
pub func:CLONE_FUEL = int32() never fails { pass 512i32; };

// How many rounds the fixed-point loop may take. A macro body may contain an
// invocation, so one pass is not enough; `macro:m = () { #m(); };` never settles,
// which is what this refuses.
pub func:EXPAND_ROUNDS = int32() never fails pure { pass 32i32; };

// A macro, found by name AND by the module that declared it. One entry per
// `macro:` declaration in the program.
//
// A MACRO'S REACH IS EXACTLY ITS MODULE (D-124). It is not exported, not reached
// by `use`, and not visible to a module nested inside the one that declares it.
// The reason is hygiene: an identifier in a macro body resolves where the macro
// was WRITTEN (D-057), and confining the invocation to that same module makes the
// defining scope and the landing scope the same scope. A macro that could cross a
// module boundary would need every later pass to carry a second scope alongside
// the one it is walking — for a form nothing in the corpus writes, since not one
// of the prototype's twenty-five macro declarations is `pub`.
pub struct:MacroEntry = {
    int32:name;     // intern index
    int32:decl;     // the `MacroDecl` node
    int32:owner;    // the module declaration it is a member of
};

pub struct:MacroTable = {
    List<MacroEntry>:v;
};

// WHERE A MACRO BODY WAS INSTANTIATED, so that a diagnostic landing inside one can
// say so.
//
// THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES, stated in `MACRO_REFERENCE.md` §10 and left open by
// 0.6.1: a node in an expanded body was WRITTEN in the macro and INSTANTIATED at
// the call site, and its span carries only the first. So "cannot find `only_local`
// in the scope this macro was written in" reports the line of the macro BODY —
// true, and about a declaration the reader may not have written — while the line
// that made it wrong is the invocation, which appears nowhere.
//
// A SPAN RANGE RATHER THAN A MARK ON EVERY NODE. A diagnostic is a source location,
// not a node handle, so mapping one back to its expansion has to be done in source
// terms: a macro body occupies a contiguous run of lines, and a diagnostic inside
// that run came out of that body. Marking nodes would need a third per-node array
// and would still not answer the question a REPORT asks.
//
// ONE ENTRY PER INSTANTIATION, not per macro. A body expanded twice has two
// invocation sites and only one of them may be at fault, so the reader gets both
// and can tell — which is more useful than a note that names the macro and leaves
// them to find its uses.
pub struct:MacroSite = {
    int32:file;      // the file the BODY lives in
    int32:lo;        // first line of the body, inclusive
    int32:hi;        // last line, inclusive
    Span:site;       // where it was invoked
};

pub struct:SiteTable = {
    List<MacroSite>:v;
};

pub func:sitetable_init = SiteTable() never fails {
    pass SiteTable{ v: raw list_init::<MacroSite>(16i64) };
};

func:sitetable_add = NIL(SiteTable->:t, MacroSite:e) never fails {
    drop list_push(@t.v, e);
    pass NIL;
};

pub struct:Expander = {
    Ast->:ast;
    InternTable->:interns;
    DiagList->:diags;
    MacroTable:macros;
    SiteTable:sites;

    // THE ARGUMENTS OF THE INVOCATION BEING INSTANTIATED, and the parameters they
    // bind to. A clone consults these at every identifier: a name that is a
    // parameter becomes the argument's subtree, and every other name is copied.
    int32:params_start;
    int32:params_count;
    int32:args_start;
    int32:args_count;

    // THE MODULE BEING EXPANDED. A macro is invocable only in the module that
    // declares it (D-124), so every lookup is a lookup in this one.
    int32:cur_module;

    // Set when a bound was exceeded, so the caller stops rather than looping.
    bool:blown;

    // THE WALK'S DEPTH (DEF-150's c2, 1.6.1e step 2): the node `expand_in_expr` or
    // `expand_in_stmt` is looking at sits this deep below its declaration's root
    // (a function's body block is 1), so a splice there knows how deep its clone
    // lands.
    int32:depth;

    // THE PROBE (DEF-173, 1.6.1e step 3). When the rounds reach their bound the
    // driver takes one more walk that instantiates NOTHING: every place that
    // would instantiate records the invocation it found instead, and the first
    // one recorded is where the refusal points. `standing` is that invocation's
    // expression id, 0 while none has been met.
    bool:probing;
    int32:standing;

    // WHERE AN ARGUMENT BEING SUBSTITUTED WAS WRITTEN (D-340; DEF-183 part B).
    // `in_arg` counts the `clone_arg` calls in progress: what is cloned inside one
    // is the caller's own text. `at_decl_site` says the instantiation in progress
    // is a declaration macro's -- its invocation stands at module level, so its
    // arguments resolve in the module's scope -- and `mod_depth` counts the
    // modules that macro's body has emitted around the point being cloned, each
    // of which an argument's name has to step back out of.
    int32:in_arg;
    bool:at_decl_site;
    int32:mod_depth;
};

pub func:macrotable_init = MacroTable() never fails {
    pass MacroTable{ v: raw list_init::<MacroEntry>(16i64) };
};

pub func:macrotable_add = NIL(MacroTable->:t, int32:name, int32:decl,
                              int32:owner) never fails {
    MacroEntry:e = MacroEntry{ name: name, decl: decl, owner: owner };
    drop list_push(@t.v, e);
    pass NIL;
};

// The macro a name refers to, or -1.
//
// LAST DECLARATION WINS IS NOT THE RULE — the first is returned, and a duplicate
// is a name declared twice, which the resolver already refuses for every other
// declaration kind. Nothing here needs to arbitrate.
pub func:macrotable_find = int32(MacroTable->:t, int32:name, int32:owner) never fails {
    int64:i = 0i64;
    while (i < t.v.count) decreases t.v.count - i {
        MacroEntry:e = t.v[i];
        if (e.name == name) {
            if (e.owner == owner) { pass e.decl; }
        }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

// THE SAME NAME, DECLARED SOMEWHERE ELSE. Asked only after the lookup above has
// failed, and only so the refusal can say WHICH of the two things went wrong: a
// name nobody declared and a name declared in another module read identically
// otherwise, and they are unrelated mistakes.
pub func:macrotable_find_elsewhere = bool(MacroTable->:t, int32:name) never fails {
    int64:i = 0i64;
    while (i < t.v.count) decreases t.v.count - i {
        if ((t.v[i]).name == name) { pass true; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    pass false;
};

func:expand_err = NIL(Expander->:x, move string:code, move string:msg, Span:sp) never fails {
    drop diaglist_push(x.diags, raw diag_error(move(code), move(msg), sp));
    pass NIL;
};

// --- substitution ------------------------------------------------------------
//
// WHICH PARAMETER A NAME IS, or -1. Substitution is by NAME and the binding is
// positional: parameter `i` takes argument `i`.
func:param_index = int32(Expander->:x, int32:name) never fails {
    int32:i = 0i32;
    while (i < x.params_count) decreases x.params_count - i {
        if ((raw ast_id_at(x.ast, x.params_start, i)) == name) { pass i; }
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

// The argument bound to a parameter, or the none expression when the invocation
// passed fewer arguments than the macro declares. ARITY IS CHECKED AT THE
// INVOCATION rather than here, so this cannot be reached with a bad index in a
// program that was accepted.
func:param_arg = ExprId(Expander->:x, int32:idx) never fails {
    if (idx < 0i32)             { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    if (idx >= x.args_count)    { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, x.args_start, idx) };
    pass a;
};

// --- cloning ------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// AN INSTANTIATION IS A COPY OF THE BODY WITH ARGUMENTS SUBSTITUTED, and it has to
// be a copy: two invocations of one macro substitute different arguments, so
// sharing the body's nodes would make the second rewrite the first.
//
// THE CLONE IS TOTAL OR IT IS SILENT. A node kind with no case here would be
// dropped from the instantiation — not diagnosed, dropped — and the program would
// compile as though the macro had emitted less than it said. So every kind is
// reached explicitly and an unclassified one reports `MACRO_INTERNAL`, which is the
// same answer `check_stmt` and `resolve_expr` give for the same situation.

// THE CLONE CARRIES THE HYGIENE MARKS OF THE NODE IT COPIES (D-340; DEF-221).
// A clone is a fresh node and its flag word starts empty, so until this stood
// here whatever the original was marked with stayed behind: `#caller(n)` written
// in an inner invocation's ARGUMENT was consumed into a marked identifier when
// the outer body was cloned, lost the mark when the inner macro cloned its
// argument, and bound in the module's scope -- RESOLVE-002, or beside a module
// binding of that spelling the module's value, in silence. The same holds for
// an argument's own marks when it is handed down a second macro level. One
// place, after the kind dispatch, so no arm can forget. (A parameter is not
// copied but REPLACED, and its replacement is marked by `clone_arg`.)
func:clone_expr = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    ExprNode:n0 = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (n0.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        if ((raw param_index(x, (raw expr_name(n0)) =>! int32)) >= 0i32) {
            pass (raw clone_expr_node(x, id, fuel));
        }
    }
    ExprId:out = raw clone_expr_node(x, id, fuel);
    if (raw expr_is_none(out)) { pass out; }
    int32:carried = (raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, id)) & (raw HYG_CARRY());
    if (carried != 0i32) {
        drop ast_set_expr_marks(x.ast, out, (raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, out)) | carried);
    }
    pass out;
};

func:clone_expr_node = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (fuel <= 0i32) {
        // ONE FAILURE, ONE DIAGNOSTIC. A body deep enough to exhaust the fuel
        // exhausts it on several branches, and each would report the same sentence
        // about the same body — the rule 0.6.4 settled for the fold budget, which
        // is the same failure through the other door.
        if (x.blown) { pass (raw expr_none()); }
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this macro body nests deeper than expansion will follow", n.span);
        x.blown = true;
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;

    // A NAME THAT IS A PARAMETER BECOMES THE ARGUMENT'S SUBTREE. Substitution is
    // not textual: the argument is an AST node and lands as one, which is why
    // `#make_const(42i32)` emits a literal rather than the characters `42i32`.
    //
    // THE ARGUMENT IS CLONED TOO. One argument used twice in a body must become two
    // subtrees, for the same reason the body must.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        int32:pi = raw param_index(x, (raw expr_name(n)) =>! int32);
        if (pi >= 0i32) {
            pass (raw clone_arg(x, raw param_arg(x, pi), f));
        }
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, n.a, n.b, n.c, n.payload));
    }

    // A CAST CARRIES A TYPE, and the type is part of the body (DEF-189). The shape
    // table calls the three kinds one-operand, which is right for every walker that
    // follows EXPRESSIONS and wrong for the clone: slot `b` -- a `dyn` cast's
    // window -- was copied through with the node, so `x =>! int32[N]->` kept the
    // template's `int32[N]` in every instantiation. Their own arms, ahead of the
    // shape dispatch.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)) {
        ExprId:cop = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), f);
        TypeId:cty = raw clone_type(x, raw expr_cast_type(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, cop.index, cty.index, n.c, n.payload));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDynCastExpr) {
        ExprId:dop = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n), f);
        IdSpan:dw = raw clone_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                            raw expr_list_count(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, dop.index, dw.start, dw.count, n.payload));
    }

    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);

    // A LEAF CARRIES ITS WIDTH, and `ast_add_expr` does not take one — it sets
    // `WNone`, which is the encoding for "this literal was written without a
    // suffix". So a cloned `3i32` came out as a cloned `3`, and the only place that
    // showed was where nothing supplied a context type: `#doubled(3i32) +
    // #doubled(10i32)` reported "this literal has no width suffix" about a literal
    // that plainly had one. Declaration position hid it completely, because a
    // `pass` takes its type from the function's return type.
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF())) {
        pass (raw ast_add_expr_w(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, n.a, n.b, n.c,
                                   n.payload, n.width));
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) {
        ExprId:a = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, a.index, n.b, n.c, n.payload));
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) {
        ExprId:a = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
        ExprId:b = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, a.index, b.index, n.c, n.payload));
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_THREE())) {
        ExprId:a = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
        ExprId:b = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n), f);
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_third(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, a.index, b.index, c.index, n.payload));
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        IdSpan:w = raw clone_expr_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                           raw expr_list_count(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, n.a, w.start, w.count, n.payload));
    }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        ExprId:a = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
        IdSpan:w = raw clone_expr_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                           raw expr_list_count(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, a.index, w.start, w.count, n.payload));
    }

    // THE FOUR CUSTOM SHAPES, each reached by name. A `CallExpr`'s window holds
    // generic arguments first and value arguments after — both are cloned, and the
    // generics are TYPES, which is why this cannot go through the expression
    // window helper.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        pass (raw clone_call(x, n, raw expr_generic_count(n), f));
    }
    // A BUILTIN'S LAYOUT IS THE OPPOSITE OF A CALL'S — slot `a` is the generic
    // count and the payload is the name, where a call has it the other way round.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        // `#caller(NAME)` IS CONSUMED HERE, and nowhere else. It is the sole way
        // for a macro body to reach the invocation site (D-057), and the clone is
        // the only moment at which "inside a macro body" is a fact rather than a
        // guess — so one that survives to the audit was written somewhere it means
        // nothing, and is refused there.
        if (raw is_caller_form(x, n)) {
            // AND AN ARGUMENT IS NOT A MACRO BODY (DEF-222). What `clone_arg`
            // clones was written at an invocation; a `#caller` inside it that a
            // body's own clone has not already consumed was written OUTSIDE every
            // macro body, where the form means nothing (MACRO-008). Until D-340
            // it was consumed here like a body's and read the caller's name --
            // `#twice(#caller(x))` in ordinary code compiled.
            if (x.in_arg > 0i32) {
                drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_CALLER_FORM(),
                    "`#caller` is legal only inside a macro body, where it names something at the invocation site; an argument is the caller's own text and names the caller's scope already (D-340)",
                    n.span);
                pass (raw expr_none());
            }
            pass (raw clone_caller(x, n));
        }
        pass (raw clone_call(x, n, raw builtin_generic_count(n), f));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        pass (raw clone_struct_literal(x, n, f));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        ExprId:sel = raw clone_expr(x, raw pickx_selector(n), f);
        IdSpan:arms = raw clone_stmt_window(x, raw pickx_arm_start(n),
                                              raw pickx_arm_count(n), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, sel.index,
                                 arms.start, arms.count, n.payload));
    }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this expression kind has no entry in the macro clone, so a macro body containing one would be silently emitted incomplete",
        n.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass (raw expr_none());
};

// IS THIS `#caller(...)`? By name only — whether the FORM is well built is
// `clone_caller`'s question, and answering both here would make a malformed
// `#caller` silently clone as an ordinary builtin instead of being reported.
pub func:is_caller_form = bool(Expander->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) { pass false; }
    string:t = raw intern_get(x.interns, raw builtin_name(n));
    pass (raw string_eq(t, "caller"));
};

// `#caller(NAME)` BECOMES A BARE IDENTIFIER, MARKED. The mark is the whole
// mechanism: the node sits lexically at the invocation site, and `HYG_CALLER` is
// what tells the resolver to bind it there rather than in the scope the enclosing
// expansion switched to.
//
// The argument is copied by NAME rather than cloned, and that is deliberate:
// `#caller(x)` names something in the caller's scope, so substituting a macro
// parameter into it would be resolving the caller's name against the macro's
// arguments — the one direction hygiene exists to prevent.
func:clone_caller = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    int32:gc = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
    int32:total = raw expr_list_count(n);
    if (gc != 0i32) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_CALLER_FORM(),
            "`#caller` takes no generic arguments; it names something at the invocation site, and a name has no type parameters",
            n.span);
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    if (total != 1i32) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_CALLER_FORM(),
            "`#caller` takes exactly one argument, the name to resolve at the invocation site",
            n.span);
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), 0i32) };
    ExprNode:anode = raw ast_expr(x.ast, a);
    if (anode.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_CALLER_FORM(),
            "`#caller` takes a bare name; an expression written here would be evaluated in the macro's scope, which is the scope it exists to escape",
            n.span);
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    ExprId:out = raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr, anode.span,
                                    0i32, 0i32, 0i32, anode.payload);
    drop ast_set_expr_flag(x.ast, out, raw HYG_CALLER());
    pass out;
};

// AN ARGUMENT IS CLONED IN THE CALLER'S SUBSTITUTION CONTEXT, WHICH IS NONE.
// The argument was written at the invocation site, so its identifiers are the
// caller's and must not be substituted again — a parameter named `x` and an
// argument mentioning `x` are different `x`es.
//
// AND ITS ROOT IS MARKED WITH HOW FAR OUT IT WAS WRITTEN (D-340; DEF-183 part B).
// The comment above was true of the clone and false of the program: the resolver
// then bound the argument's names where the BODY's are bound, in the module's
// scope. So a caller's local could not be passed (`#twice(n)`: RESOLVE-002), one
// that shadowed a module binding was replaced by it in silence (200 for 10), a
// local the body declared captured it (`int32:tmp = 1i32; ... tmp + X` with the
// caller's `tmp` passed: 2 for 8), and so did a parameter of a function a
// declaration macro emitted. The mark is on the ROOT and counts sites, because
// an argument may bind names of its own (a `pick` arm's) and may itself hold an
// invocation: what is under it resolves as it would have at the invocation.
//
//   an expression or statement macro's argument: ONE more step back -- out of
//     the expansion it is substituted into;
//   a declaration macro's argument: `HYG_SITE`, and one step back for each
//     module the macro's body has emitted around this point.
//
// The clone carried whatever the argument's root already had (an argument that
// is exactly an enclosing macro's parameter has stepped in once already), so
// the steps add.
func:clone_arg = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:ps = x.params_start;
    int32:pc = x.params_count;
    x.params_count = 0i32;
    x.in_arg = x.in_arg + 1i32;
    ExprId:out = raw clone_expr(x, id, fuel);
    x.in_arg = x.in_arg - 1i32;
    x.params_start = ps;
    x.params_count = pc;
    if (raw expr_is_none(out)) { pass out; }

    int32:word = raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, out);
    int32:back = raw hyg_back(word);
    if (x.at_decl_site) {
        back = back + x.mod_depth;
        word = word | (raw HYG_SITE());
    } else {
        back = back + 1i32;
    }
    if (back > (raw HYG_COUNT_MAX())) {
        if (!x.blown) {
            ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(x.ast, out);
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
                "this argument has been handed down more macro levels than expansion will follow (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
                an.span);
        }
        x.blown = true;
        pass (raw expr_none());
    }
    drop ast_set_expr_marks(x.ast, out, raw hyg_with(word, back, raw hyg_roots(word)));
    pass out;
};

// SHARED BY BOTH CALL SHAPES, with the generic count passed IN rather than read
// here — because the two kinds keep it in different slots and a clone that read it
// itself would have to know which, which is the coupling that caused the defect
// this parameter exists to avoid.
func:clone_call = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprNode:n, int32:gc, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:start = raw expr_list_start(n);
    int32:total = raw expr_list_count(n);

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    int32:i = 0i32;
    while (i < gc) decreases gc - i {
        // The generic arguments are TYPES, cloned as every type in a body is
        // (`clone_type`: shared when it holds no expression). They were copied
        // through until DEF-189 -- `#size_of<int32[N]>()` kept the template's
        // `N` in every instantiation, whatever the argument.
        TypeId:gt = raw clone_type(x, TypeId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gt.index);
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    while (i < total) decreases total - i {
        ExprId:a = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, a, fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);

    // A CALL'S slot `a` IS ITS CALLEE; a builtin's is its generic count, and a
    // builtin has no callee expression — `expr_callee` on one reads the count as an
    // index, which `expr_is_none` then answers `false` to. So the slot is rebuilt
    // from what the node already had rather than from a clone.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, n.a, w.start, w.count, n.payload));
    }
    ExprId:callee = raw clone_expr(x, raw expr_callee(n), fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, callee.index,
                             w.start, w.count, n.payload));
};

// A struct literal's window alternates NAME, VALUE — the names are field intern
// indices and only the odd entries are expressions.
func:clone_struct_literal = ExprId(Expander->:x, ExprNode:n, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:start = raw expr_list_start(n);
    int32:cnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cnt) {
        if ((i % 2i32) == 0i32) {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i));
        } else {
            ExprId:v = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
            ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, v, fuel);
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
        }
    }
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    pass (raw ast_add_expr(x.ast, n.kind, n.span, n.a, w.start, w.count, n.payload));
};

func:clone_expr_window = IdSpan(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        ExprId:e = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, e, fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
    }
    pass (raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark));
};

// --- cloning statements --------------------------------------------------------
//
// TWENTY-FIVE KINDS, EACH REACHED BY NAME. There is no `stmt_shape` table the way
// there is for expressions, so this cannot be driven generically — and the
// consequence of a missing case is not a wrong answer but a SILENTLY SHORTER
// program, which is why the fall-through reports rather than returns.

// A statement's marks are carried as an expression's are (`clone_expr`): the
// block an expansion left behind is an expansion still when it is cloned.
func:clone_stmt = StmtId(Expander->:x, StmtId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass (raw stmt_none()); }
    StmtId:out = raw clone_stmt_node(x, id, fuel);
    if (raw stmt_is_none(out)) { pass out; }
    int32:carried = (raw ast_stmt_marks(x.ast, id)) & (raw HYG_CARRY());
    if (carried != 0i32) {
        drop ast_set_stmt_marks(x.ast, out, (raw ast_stmt_marks(x.ast, out)) | carried);
    }
    pass out;
};

func:clone_stmt_node = StmtId(Expander->:x, StmtId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass (raw stmt_none()); }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);
    if (fuel <= 0i32) {
        // ONE FAILURE, ONE DIAGNOSTIC. A body deep enough to exhaust the fuel
        // exhausts it on several branches, and each would report the same sentence
        // about the same body — the rule 0.6.4 settled for the fold budget, which
        // is the same failure through the other door.
        if (x.blown) { pass (raw stmt_none()); }
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this macro body nests deeper than expansion will follow", s.span);
        x.blown = true;
        pass (raw stmt_none());
    }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        IdSpan:w = raw clone_stmt_window(x, raw stmt_list_start(s),
                                           raw stmt_list_count(s), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, s.a, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        // THE DECLARED TYPE AND THE ATTRIBUTES ARE CLONED (DEF-189): `int32[N]:a`
        // is the declaration this defect was found on.
        TypeId:vty = raw clone_type(x, raw stmt_decl_type(s), f);
        ExprId:init = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s), f);
        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, init.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, raw stmt_quals(x.ast, s));
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_decl_limit(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        int32:ac = raw stmt_decl_attr_count(x.ast, s);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
        for (int32:i in 0i32...ac) {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_attr(x, raw stmt_decl_attr(x.ast, s, i), f)).index);
        }
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, vty.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        ExprId:t = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_target(s), f);
        ExprId:v = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_assigned(s), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, t.index, v.index, s.c, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        StmtId:t = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s), f);
        StmtId:e = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, c.index, t.index, e.index, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), f);
        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, b.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_while_invariant(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_while_measure(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, c.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        // THE BINDING IS A DECLARATION AND IS CLONED (DEF-189): the resolver
        // declares the loop's name with this node as its origin, and until this
        // step every instantiation's loop declared its own symbol over ONE node.
        DeclId:fb = raw clone_param(x, raw stmt_for_binding(s), f);
        ExprId:it = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_for_iter(x.ast, s), f);
        StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s), f);
        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, it.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, b.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_for_invariant(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_for_measure(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, fb.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s), f);
        StmtId:t = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s), f);
        StmtId:e = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s), f);
        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, b.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, t.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, e.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_when_invariant(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_when_measure(x.ast, s), f)).index);
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, c.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) { pass (raw clone_counted(x, s, f)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt) { pass (raw clone_counted(x, s, f)); }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        ExprId:sel = raw clone_expr(x, raw pick_selector(s), f);
        IdSpan:w = raw clone_stmt_window(x, raw pick_arm_start(s),
                                           raw pick_arm_count(s), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, sel.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) {
        // THE PATTERN IS CLONED (DEF-189). It was copied through -- "a form the
        // corpus does not exercise" -- so a parameter written as a pattern's value
        // or a range's bound was never replaced, and beside a module binding of
        // that spelling the arm silently matched the binding.
        PatId:ap = raw clone_pat(x, raw arm_pattern(s), f);
        ExprId:g = raw clone_expr(x, raw arm_guard(s), f);
        StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, ap.index, g.index, b.index, s.payload));
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: s.a }, f);
        pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, b.index, s.b, s.c, s.payload));
    }

    // `break`, `continue` and `fall` carry a LABEL and nothing to clone.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)    { pass (raw clone_leaf_stmt(x, s)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) { pass (raw clone_leaf_stmt(x, s)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt)     { pass (raw clone_leaf_stmt(x, s)); }

    // One expression in slot `a`: `pass`, `fail`, `return`, `exit`, and the six
    // that `stmt_carries_expr` names.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt)   { pass (raw clone_operand_stmt(x, s, f)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)   { pass (raw clone_operand_stmt(x, s, f)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) { pass (raw clone_operand_stmt(x, s, f)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)   { pass (raw clone_operand_stmt(x, s, f)); }
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind))     { pass (raw clone_operand_stmt(x, s, f)); }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this statement kind has no entry in the macro clone, so a macro body containing one would be silently emitted incomplete",
        s.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass (raw stmt_none());
};

func:clone_leaf_stmt = StmtId(Expander->:x, StmtNode:s) never fails {
    pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, s.a, s.b, s.c, s.payload));
};

func:clone_operand_stmt = StmtId(Expander->:x, StmtNode:s, int32:fuel) never fails {
    ExprId:e = raw clone_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a }, fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, e.index, s.b, s.c, s.payload));
};

// A VERIFICATION NODE IS CLONED PER EXPANSION (1.5.1, V-19). Until then every
// site copied the VerifyId INDEX, so all expansions of a macro shared one node
// and one condition expression with the template and with each other — and
// resolution writes an identifier's binding onto the shared node, so the LAST
// expansion resolved won, and the first expansion's contract named the last
// expansion's parameter symbol. Invisible while the backend refused the whole
// family as a rung; a miscompile the day 1.5.3 lowers a contract inside a
// macro-emitted function. A limit is a leaf (its binding slot is written by
// resolve, after this), `never fails` and `gives` are markers; a contract and a
// `joins` clause carry one expression, an invariant a window.
func:clone_verify = VerifyId(Expander->:x, VerifyId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(id)) { pass (raw verify_none()); }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(x.ast, id);
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) {
        ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, raw contract_cond(v), fuel);
        pass (raw ast_add_verify(x.ast, v.kind, v.span, v.a, c.index, v.c, v.payload));
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyJoinsWithin) {
        ExprId:jd = raw clone_expr(x, raw contract_cond(v), fuel);
        pass (raw ast_add_verify(x.ast, v.kind, v.span, v.a, jd.index, v.c, v.payload));
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyInvariantNode) {
        IdSpan:w = raw clone_expr_window(x, raw invariant_start(v),
                                           raw invariant_count(v), fuel);
        pass (raw ast_add_verify(x.ast, v.kind, v.span, v.a, w.start, w.count, v.payload));
    }
    // A MEASURE (D-304, 1.5.8c) carries one expression, or none under `unbounded`.
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyDecreasesNode) {
        ExprId:me = raw measure_expr(v);
        int32:mi = 0i32;
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(me))) { mi = (raw clone_expr(x, me, fuel)).index; }
        pass (raw ast_add_verify(x.ast, v.kind, v.span, v.a, mi, v.c, v.payload));
    }
    pass (raw ast_add_verify(x.ast, v.kind, v.span, v.a, v.b, v.c, v.payload));
};

// --- types, patterns, attributes, generic parameters (DEF-189, 1.6.1e step 3a) --------
//
// SUBSTITUTION TRAVERSES THE WHOLE EMITTED SUBTREE (MACRO_REFERENCE §3), and what a
// body writes inside a TYPE, a PATTERN, an ATTRIBUTE or a GENERIC PARAMETER is part
// of it. Until this step each of those was copied through by id -- "a form the
// corpus does not exercise, and substituting into one silently would be inventing a
// rule" -- so a parameter written in one was never replaced and resolved as the
// bare name: beside a module binding of that spelling the body SILENTLY READ THE
// BINDING. `macro:mk = (N) { int32[N]:a = …; };` beside `fixed int32:N = 2i32;`
// built a two-element array for `#mk(3i32)` -- exit 8 where 12 is right, at both
// legs, on every compiler to that day. The rule was never missing; §3 states it.
//
// WHAT IS SHARED AND WHAT IS NOT is settled by one question, asked of each node
// kind: can two instantiations need the node to differ, or does a later pass WRITE
// onto it or key a record by it?
//
//   * an EXPRESSION, a STATEMENT, a VERIFICATION node -- cloned, as they were;
//   * a DECLARATION -- cloned, every kind. The resolver declares a symbol whose
//     origin is the node, so one node under two instantiations is two bindings
//     with one identity: a `for` binding, a generic parameter, a field, a variant
//     and an attribute were each ONE node for every instantiation until this step;
//   * a PATTERN -- cloned, every kind. The checker records a destructure's binding
//     types ON the pattern (`ast_set_pat_payload`) and the resolver keys each
//     binding's symbol by it, so a shared one is the last instantiation checked
//     winning -- 1.5.1's finding about verification nodes (`clone_verify`), in
//     another kind. Probed before this was written (two instantiations over
//     `Opt<string>` and `Opt<Two>`, consuming and lending, in either order): the
//     answers were right, because the one reader of that record reads it while
//     its own `pick` is being checked. It is cloned so that this stays a fact
//     about the tree and not about the order of a walk;
//   * a TYPE -- shared when it holds no expression, cloned when it does. Nothing
//     writes onto a type node and no table is keyed by one, and the only thing
//     inside a type that an instantiation can change is an expression -- an
//     array's size, a `comptime` argument. A type without one cannot differ, so it
//     stays the template's node. (A parameter's NAME standing where a type's name
//     stands is refused at the macro's declaration, `check_macro_decls`: an
//     argument is an expression and cannot name a type.)

// DOES THIS TYPE HOLD AN EXPRESSION, anywhere inside it? The suffix run is followed
// in a loop, as `expand_in_type` follows it and for its reason; a window recurses
// under `fuel`. Too deep to answer is answered YES: the clone then follows the
// type and refuses it by its own fuel, once.
func:type_holds_expr = bool(Expander->:x, TypeId:start, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    TypeId:cur = start;
    while (!(raw type_is_none(cur))) decreases cur.index {
        TypeNode:t = raw ast_type(x.ast, cur);
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeArrayType) {
            // `T[]` has no size; `T[N]` does.
            if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw type_array_size(t)))) { pass true; }
            cur = raw type_element(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypePointerType)  { cur = raw type_pointee(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeOptionalType) { cur = raw type_inner(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeProjection)   { cur = raw type_projection_base(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeFuncType) {
            if (raw type_window_holds_expr(x, raw type_param_start(t),
                                             raw type_param_count(t), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
            cur = raw type_return(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeComptimeArg) { pass true; }
        if ((t.kind == TypeKind.TypeNamedType) || (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeDynType)) {
            pass (raw type_window_holds_expr(x, raw type_args_start(t),
                                               raw type_args_count(t), fuel - 1i32));
        }
        // `cstring`, `any` and `Self` hold nothing.
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

func:type_window_holds_expr = bool(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count,
                                   int32:fuel) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        if (raw type_holds_expr(x, TypeId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel)) {
            pass true;
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A TYPE, CLONED WHERE IT CAN DIFFER. The same id comes back when the type holds
// no expression; otherwise every node on the path to an expression is rebuilt --
// the wrapped type first, then the node that wraps it, the order the parser builds
// them in and the order `expand_in_type`'s measure relies on -- and the expression
// goes through `clone_expr`, so a parameter in it becomes the argument, a
// `#caller(name)` the caller's name, and an invocation a clone the next round
// expands. The rebuild recurses, a frame per level, under the clone's fuel.
func:clone_type = TypeId(Expander->:x, TypeId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw type_is_none(id)) { pass (raw type_none()); }
    if (!(raw type_holds_expr(x, id, fuel))) { pass id; }
    TypeNode:t = raw ast_type(x.ast, id);
    if (fuel <= 0i32) {
        // ONE FAILURE, ONE DIAGNOSTIC -- `clone_expr`'s rule.
        if (x.blown) { pass (raw type_none()); }
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this macro body nests deeper than expansion will follow", t.span);
        x.blown = true;
        pass (raw type_none());
    }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;

    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeArrayType) {
        TypeId:el = raw clone_type(x, raw type_element(t), f);
        ExprId:size = raw clone_expr(x, raw type_array_size(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, el.index, size.index, t.c, t.payload));
    }
    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypePointerType) {
        TypeId:pt = raw clone_type(x, raw type_pointee(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, pt.index, t.b, t.c, t.payload));
    }
    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeOptionalType) {
        TypeId:ot = raw clone_type(x, raw type_inner(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, ot.index, t.b, t.c, t.payload));
    }
    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeProjection) {
        TypeId:bt = raw clone_type(x, raw type_projection_base(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, bt.index, t.b, t.c, t.payload));
    }
    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeFuncType) {
        TypeId:ret = raw clone_type(x, raw type_return(t), f);
        IdSpan:pw = raw clone_type_window(x, raw type_param_start(t),
                                            raw type_param_count(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, pw.start, pw.count, ret.index, t.payload));
    }
    if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeComptimeArg) {
        ExprId:cv = raw clone_expr(x, raw type_comptime_value(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, cv.index, t.b, t.c, t.payload));
    }
    if ((t.kind == TypeKind.TypeNamedType) || (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeDynType)) {
        IdSpan:aw = raw clone_type_window(x, raw type_args_start(t),
                                            raw type_args_count(t), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_type(x.ast, t.kind, t.span, aw.start, aw.count, t.c, t.payload));
    }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this type kind has no entry in the macro clone, so a macro body containing one would be emitted with the template's own type",
        t.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass (raw type_none());
};

// A WINDOW OF TYPES -- a named type's arguments, a function type's parameters, a
// `dyn`'s traits, a variant's payloads, a generic parameter's bounds, a trait's
// supertraits. The same window comes back when none of them holds an expression.
func:clone_type_window = IdSpan(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (!(raw type_window_holds_expr(x, start, count, fuel))) {
        pass IdSpan{ start: start, count: count };
    }
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        TypeId:c = raw clone_type(x, TypeId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
    }
    pass (raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark));
};

// A PATTERN, CLONED: a value's expression and a range's two bounds through
// `clone_expr`; a destructure's names as they are -- its windows hold intern
// indices, which nothing rewrites -- on a node of its own, with the slot the
// checker writes its binding types to (the payload) empty as the parser left it.
//
// THE PATTERN'S KIND IS THE PARSER'S AND DOES NOT CHANGE (`expand_in_pat` says why).
// So an ARGUMENT that is a range, substituted for a parameter standing as a whole
// value pattern, is refused here as the range-bodied macro is refused there: it
// would leave a range VALUE where one value is matched.
func:clone_pat = PatId(Expander->:x, PatId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw pat_is_none(id)) { pass (raw pat_none()); }
    PatNode:p = raw ast_pat(x.ast, id);
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatValue) {
        ExprId:v = raw clone_expr(x, raw pat_value(p), fuel);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(v))) {
            // (The parser never leaves a range as a value pattern's expression,
            // so a range here came in through a parameter.)
            ExprNode:now = raw ast_expr(x.ast, v);
            if (now.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
                drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
                    "this is a value pattern, and the argument substituted into it is a range: a pattern's kind is read where it is written, so an argument cannot make it a range pattern; write the range in the pattern and pass its bounds -- `(LO..HI)`",
                    p.span);
                // ONE MISTAKE, ONE REPORT (D-240): the pattern is left without a
                // value, so the walk's own check of a value pattern that holds a
                // range (`expand_in_pat`) has nothing to say a second time.
                drop blank_tree(x, v, fuel);
                v = raw expr_none();
            }
        }
        pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, v.index, p.b, p.c, 0i64));
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatRange) {
        ExprId:lo = raw clone_expr(x, raw pat_range_lo(p), fuel);
        ExprId:hi = raw clone_expr(x, raw pat_range_hi(p), fuel);
        pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, lo.index, hi.index, p.c, 0i64));
    }
    // A struct destructure names its type in `a` -- a bare name, no arguments by
    // the grammar, so no expression and the template's node -- and its bindings
    // in `b`, `c`; an enum destructure's header, segments and bindings are one
    // window in `b`, `c`.
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatStructDestructure) {
        pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, p.a, p.b, p.c, 0i64));
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatEnumDestructure) {
        pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, 0i32, p.b, p.c, 0i64));
    }
    // The wildcard and `ERR:` carry nothing.
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatWildcard)   { pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, 0i32, 0i32, 0i32, 0i64)); }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatErrPattern) { pass (raw ast_add_pat(x.ast, p.kind, p.span, 0i32, 0i32, 0i32, 0i64)); }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this pattern kind has no entry in the macro clone, so a macro body containing one would be silently emitted incomplete",
        p.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass (raw pat_none());
};

// AN ATTRIBUTE, CLONED WITH ITS ARGUMENTS -- `#[align(N)]` on whatever carries it.
func:clone_attr = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass (raw decl_none()); }
    DeclNode:a = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    IdSpan:w = raw clone_expr_window(x, raw attr_arg_start(a), raw attr_arg_count(a), fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, a.kind, a.span, a.a, w.start, w.count, a.payload));
};

// A GENERIC PARAMETER, CLONED: a `comptime` one's value type and a type one's
// bounds are types, and each may hold a size or a value argument.
func:clone_generic = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass (raw decl_none()); }
    DeclNode:g = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    TypeId:vt = raw clone_type(x, raw generic_value_type(g), fuel);
    IdSpan:w = raw clone_type_window(x, raw generic_bound_start(g),
                                       raw generic_bound_count(g), fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, g.kind, g.span, vt.index, w.start, w.count, g.payload));
};

// A PARAMETER, A `for` BINDING, A VARIADIC TAIL AND A FIELD share one layout --
// `a` the type, `b` a `limit` (none on a binding and a tail), `c` the flags, the
// payload the name -- and one clone: the type through `clone_type`, the `limit`
// through `clone_verify` (1.5.1: what resolve writes onto it belongs to this
// expansion alone), the rest as written.
func:clone_param = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass (raw decl_none()); }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    TypeId:ty = raw clone_type(x, raw param_type(d), fuel);
    VerifyId:lim = raw clone_verify(x, raw param_limit(d), fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, ty.index, lim.index, d.c, d.payload));
};

// A VARIANT: its value is an expression, its payloads are types.
func:clone_variant = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d, int32:fuel) never fails {
    ExprId:v = raw clone_expr(x, raw variant_value(d), fuel);
    IdSpan:w = raw clone_type_window(x, raw variant_payload_start(d),
                                       raw variant_payload_count(d), fuel);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, v.index, w.start, w.count, d.payload));
};

func:clone_counted = StmtId(Expander->:x, StmtNode:s, int32:fuel) never fails {
    StmtId:b = raw clone_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s), fuel);
    int32:argc = raw stmt_counted_argc(x.ast, s);
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_invariant(x.ast, s), fuel)).index);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, argc);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...argc) {
        ExprId:a = raw clone_expr(x, raw stmt_counted_arg(x.ast, s, i), fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, a.index);
    }
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_measure(x.ast, s), fuel)).index);
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    pass (raw ast_add_stmt(x.ast, s.kind, s.span, b.index, w.start, w.count, s.payload));
};

func:clone_stmt_window = IdSpan(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        StmtId:st = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) };
        StmtId:c = raw clone_stmt(x, st, fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
    }
    pass (raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark));
};

// --- cloning declarations -------------------------------------------------------
//
// WHAT A MACRO EMITS IS DECLARATIONS, so this is the case D-057 says macros exist
// for: "splicing fields into a struct and methods into an `impl`, and emitting
// mutually-referencing declarations, are things generics, `comptime`, and
// `#[derive]` cannot do."
//
// EVERYTHING A DECLARATION CARRIES IS CLONED WITH IT -- its types, its generic
// parameters, its attributes, its members -- by the rule stated above
// `type_holds_expr`: a declaration node always, a type where it can differ.
//
// (This paragraph said "types, patterns and verify nodes are copied through rather
// than cloned ... cloning them just in case would be inventing a rule about a form
// nobody has written" from 0.6.1. Verification nodes left it at 1.5.1, when one
// shared between two expansions turned out to be resolved once for both; types and
// patterns at DEF-189, when a parameter written in one turned out to be a form
// somebody writes -- and MACRO_REFERENCE §3 had stated the rule all along.)

func:clone_decl = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass (raw decl_none()); }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (fuel <= 0i32) {
        // ONE FAILURE, ONE DIAGNOSTIC. A body deep enough to exhaust the fuel
        // exhausts it on several branches, and each would report the same sentence
        // about the same body — the rule 0.6.4 settled for the fold budget, which
        // is the same failure through the other door.
        if (x.blown) { pass (raw decl_none()); }
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this macro body nests deeper than expansion will follow", d.span);
        x.blown = true;
        pass (raw decl_none());
    }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) {
        StmtId:body = raw clone_stmt(x, raw fn_body(x.ast, d), f);

        int32:gc = raw fn_generic_count(x.ast, d);
        int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(x.ast, d);
        int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(x.ast, d);
        int32:ac = raw fn_attr_count(x.ast, d);

        // THE SIGNATURE IS CLONED WITH THE BODY (DEF-189): the return type, the
        // variadic tail, and below them the generic parameters, the parameters,
        // the contracts and the attributes. A function a macro emits may take
        // `int32[N]:a` and return `int32[N]`, and each instantiation's is its own.
        TypeId:fret = raw clone_type(x, raw fn_return(x.ast, d), f);
        DeclId:fvar = raw clone_param(x, raw fn_variadic(x.ast, d), f);

        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, fret.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, body.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, fvar.index);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, pc);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, cc);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);

        // Each section by its NAMED accessor rather than by walking the window.
        // Four loops rather than one over the raw tail, because `d_at` is private
        // on purpose: a raw slot read is how a window whose sections shift silently
        // becomes a defect, and this clone would be the worst place to have one.
        int32:i = 0i32;
        while (i < gc) decreases gc - i { drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_generic(x, raw fn_generic(x.ast, d, i), f)).index); i = i + 1i32; }
        // PARAMETERS AND CONTRACTS HAVE BEEN CLONED SINCE 1.5.1 (V-19): a
        // parameter carries a `limit` and a contract carries a condition, and
        // both are nodes resolution writes onto — shared, the last expansion
        // resolved wins.
        i = 0i32;
        while (i < pc) decreases pc - i { drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_param(x, raw fn_param(x.ast, d, i), f)).index); i = i + 1i32; }
        i = 0i32;
        while (i < cc) decreases cc - i { drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw fn_contract(x.ast, d, i), f)).index); i = i + 1i32; }
        i = 0i32;
        while (i < ac) decreases ac - i { drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_attr(x, raw fn_attr(x.ast, d, i), f)).index); i = i + 1i32; }
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, d.a, w.start, w.count, d.payload));
    }

    // A FIELD, A PARAMETER AND A VARIADIC TAIL are a type, a `limit` and a name
    // (`clone_param`); a variant is a value and payload types; an attribute is its
    // arguments. Each was a flat copy until DEF-189 -- "a type and a name, with
    // nothing inside to clone" -- which shared the type, a field's `limit` and a
    // variant's value expression with the template.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl)    { pass (raw clone_param(x, id, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl)    { pass (raw clone_param(x, id, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclVariadicSpec) { pass (raw clone_param(x, id, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumVariant)  { pass (raw clone_variant(x, d, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclAttribute)    { pass (raw clone_attr(x, id, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclGenericParam) { pass (raw clone_generic(x, id, f)); }

    // A GLOBAL carries a type and an initialiser.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclGlobalDecl) {
        TypeId:gty = raw clone_type(x, raw global_type(d), f);
        ExprId:init = raw clone_expr(x, raw global_init(d), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, gty.index, init.index, d.c, d.payload));
    }

    // THE ITEM KINDS — struct, enum, trait, module — share one window shape: a
    // four-slot header, then generics, members, attributes and extras (a trait's
    // supertraits), every section cloned.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclStructDecl) { pass (raw clone_item(x, d, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumDecl)   { pass (raw clone_item(x, d, f)); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl)  { pass (raw clone_item(x, d, f)); }
    // A MODULE THE BODY EMITS IS A SCOPE OF ITS OWN, sealed from the module the
    // invocation stands in, and an argument used inside it was written OUTSIDE
    // it: `clone_arg` reads this count as the steps back out (D-340).
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
        x.mod_depth = x.mod_depth + 1i32;
        DeclId:mc = raw clone_item(x, d, f);
        x.mod_depth = x.mod_depth - 1i32;
        pass mc;
    }

    // AN `impl` IS NOT AN ITEM. Five header slots against four, and in a different
    // order — so cloning one through `clone_item` read the trait's type id as the
    // member count. Shipped in 0.6.1 and never fired, because it takes a macro body
    // containing an `impl` to reach, and none of the tests had one.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) { pass (raw clone_impl(x, d, f)); }

    // A `Rules` BLOCK IN A MACRO BODY (1.5.1): its refinements are verification
    // nodes and its clauses are expressions, both cloned, and its subject is a
    // type, cloned like every type (DEF-189). Until 1.5.1 this kind fell to the
    // fail-closed default below — refused loudly, never silently — and it gains
    // an arm here because its bodies are typed now (D-220).
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclRuleDecl) {
        TypeId:rsub = raw clone_type(x, raw rule_subject(d), f);
        int32:rn = raw rule_refine_count(x.ast, d);
        int32:cn = raw rule_clause_count(x.ast, d);
        int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, rn);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, cn);
        for (int32:ri in 0i32...rn) {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_verify(x, raw rule_refine(x.ast, d, ri), f)).index);
        }
        for (int32:ci in 0i32...cn) {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_expr(x, raw rule_clause(x.ast, d, ci), f)).index);
        }
        IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
        // THE FLAGS RIDE THE HIGH HALF OF THE COUNT SLOT (DEF-93), as the parser
        // builds the node. Until DEF-189's reading this wrote the bare count, so
        // a `pub Rules` block that a macro emitted lost its `pub` on the way out.
        pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, rsub.index, w.start,
                                 w.count | ((raw decl_flags(d)) << 16i32), d.payload));
    }

    // A NESTED INVOCATION IS COPIED THROUGH AND EXPANDS ON THE NEXT ROUND. That is
    // what makes the fixed point a fixed point rather than a single pass: `#outer()`
    // emitting `#inner()` leaves an invocation behind, and the loop comes back for
    // it.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) {
        ExprId:inv = raw clone_expr(x, raw splice_invocation(d), f);
        pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, inv.index, d.b, d.c, d.payload));
    }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this declaration kind has no entry in the macro clone, so a macro body containing one would be silently emitted incomplete",
        d.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass (raw decl_none());
};

func:clone_impl = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:gc = raw impl_generic_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:mc = raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ac = raw impl_attr_count(x.ast, d);

    // Target and trait are types, cloned as every type in a body is (DEF-189).
    TypeId:itgt = raw clone_type(x, raw impl_target(x.ast, d), fuel);
    TypeId:itr = raw clone_type(x, raw impl_trait(x.ast, d), fuel);

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, itgt.index);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, itr.index);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, mc);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);

    for (int32:g in 0i32...gc) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_generic(x, raw impl_generic(x.ast, d, g), fuel)).index);
    }
    for (int32:m in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclId:c = raw clone_decl(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, m), fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
    }
    for (int32:a2 in 0i32...ac) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_attr(x, raw impl_attr(x.ast, d, a2), fuel)).index);
    }
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, d.a, w.start, w.count, d.payload));
};

func:clone_item = DeclId(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d, int32:fuel) never fails {
    int32:gc = raw item_generic_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:mc = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ac = raw item_attr_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ec = raw item_extra_count(x.ast, d);

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, mc);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ec);

    for (int32:i in 0i32...gc) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_generic(x, raw item_generic(x.ast, d, i), fuel)).index);
    }
    for (int32:m in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclId:c = raw clone_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d, m), fuel);
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
    }
    for (int32:a2 in 0i32...ac) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_attr(x, raw item_attr(x.ast, d, a2), fuel)).index);
    }
    // The extras are a trait's supertraits: types.
    for (int32:e2 in 0i32...ec) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw clone_type(x, raw item_extra(x.ast, d, e2), fuel)).index);
    }
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, d.kind, d.span, d.a, w.start, w.count, d.payload));
};

// --- invocations inside a body ----------------------------------------------------
//
// EXPANSION AT MODULE LEVEL WAS ONLY ONE OF THE FOUR POSITIONS. `#name()` also
// stands as a STATEMENT and as an EXPRESSION, and until this existed neither
// expanded — a `#doubled(3i32)` in a function body stayed a `BuiltinExpr` that
// nothing validated, nothing typed and nothing walked. It reached the end of the
// frontend as the INVALID type, which is silent by design, so a program full of
// invocations that did nothing at all checked clean.
//
// SUBSTITUTION IS IN PLACE. An expression can sit anywhere in an arbitrarily deep
// expression, so rebuilding the tree above it would mean reconstructing every
// ancestor up to the enclosing statement. `ast_replace_expr` writes the expansion
// over the invocation instead, which leaves every window in the program untouched.

// The macro this expression invokes, or -1. Silent: `#size_of<T>()` is a builtin
// and not a macro, and telling those apart is the AUDIT's job at the end, once
// every round has had its chance to expand.
func:macro_here = int32(Expander->:x, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.kind != ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    pass (raw macrotable_find(@x.macros, raw builtin_name(n), x.cur_module));
};

// ARITY, AND THE BINDING IT ESTABLISHES. Returns whether the invocation may be
// instantiated; on `true` the expander's substitution context is the invocation's.
func:bind_invocation = bool(Expander->:x, DeclNode:md, ExprNode:inv, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:pcount = raw macro_param_count(x.ast, md);
    int32:gcount = raw builtin_generic_count(inv);
    int32:acount = (raw expr_list_count(inv)) - gcount;
    if (acount != pcount) {
        string:n1 = string_concat("`#", raw intern_get(x.interns,
                                                              raw builtin_name(inv)));
        string:n2 = string_concat(n1, "` takes ");
        string:n3 = string_concat(n2, int_to_string(pcount => int64));
        string:n4 = string_concat(n3, " argument(s) and this passes ");
        string:n5 = string_concat(n4, int_to_string(acount => int64));
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_ARITY(), move(n5), at);
        pass false;
    }
    x.params_start = (raw macro_param_span(x.ast, md)).start;
    x.params_count = pcount;
    x.args_start = (raw expr_list_start(inv)) + gcount;
    x.args_count = acount;
    pass true;
};

// DETACHED, AND BLANKED. Once an invocation is instantiated its own subtree is
// referenced by nothing — the arguments were CLONED into the body, so the
// originals are dead. Two whole-array audits would read a dead identifier as an
// unbound one, so the expander says so rather than leaving them to be guessed at.
//
// Driven by `expr_shape` and the four custom kinds, exactly like the clone. A kind
// this misses leaves a live-looking dead node rather than corrupting anything, so
// it reports and carries on instead of blowing the expansion.
//
// WHAT THE CLONE CLONES IS DETACHED WITH THE ORIGINAL, AND WHAT IT SHARES HOLDS NO
// EXPRESSION (DEF-189). A type -- a cast's target, a turbofish's or a builtin's
// generic arguments -- is cloned exactly when it holds an expression, so the
// original's expressions are dead with the rest of the original and are blanked
// (`blank_type`); a type the clone shared has none to blank. An argument the body
// never mentions goes the same way, its inner invocations with it: never
// expanded, never audited -- `#ignore(#size_of<int32[#n()]>())` is a correct
// program that drops `#n()`.
//
// (From DEF-170 until DEF-189 a type was the same node in the original and in
// every clone, so it could not be blanked and was WALKED here instead, where it
// stood -- which expanded an invocation inside a type in place, once, for every
// instantiation that shared it.)
func:blank_tree = NIL(Expander->:x, ExprId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprNone) { pass NIL; }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;
    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        drop blank_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_generic_count(n), f);
        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_callee(n), f);
        drop blank_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw expr_generic_count(n)),
                          (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw expr_generic_count(n)), f);
    } else {
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
            drop blank_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw builtin_generic_count(n), f);
            drop blank_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw builtin_generic_count(n)),
                              (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw builtin_generic_count(n)), f);
        } else {
            if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
                int32:cnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
                int32:i = 1i32;
                while (i < cnt) decreases cnt - i {
                    drop blank_tree(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast,
                                     raw expr_list_start(n), i) }, f);
                    i = i + 2i32;
                }
            } else {
                if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
                    // THE ARMS ARE BLANKED TOO (DEF-170). They were left whole
                    // ("a form nothing writes"), so an invocation in an arm of an
                    // expression-`pick` handed to a macro stood in the dead
                    // original after the clone had taken its place, and the
                    // audit refused it as a hole: `#id(pick (n) { (1i32) { give
                    // #one(); }, … })`, MACRO-006 in a correct program.
                    drop blank_tree(x, raw pickx_selector(n), f);
                    drop blank_stmt_window(x, raw pickx_arm_start(n),
                                           raw pickx_arm_count(n), f);
                } else {
                    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)) {
                        drop blank_type(x, raw expr_cast_type(n), f);
                    }
                    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDynCastExpr) {
                        drop blank_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                               raw expr_list_count(n), f);
                    }
                    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
                        drop blank_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                          raw expr_list_count(n), f);
                    }
                    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) {
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
                    }
                    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
                        drop blank_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                          raw expr_list_count(n), f);
                    }
                    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_TWO())) {
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_rhs(n), f);
                    }
                    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_THREE())) {
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_lhs(n), f);
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_rhs(n), f);
                        drop blank_tree(x, raw expr_third(n), f);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
    drop ast_blank_expr(x.ast, id);
    pass NIL;
};

func:blank_window = NIL(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        drop blank_tree(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE STATEMENTS OF A DETACHED ARGUMENT -- an expression-`pick`'s arms and what
// their bodies hold. EVERY EXPRESSION THE CLONE CLONES IS BLANKED, kind by kind as
// `clone_stmt` reads them, a verification node's among them (the clone makes a
// new node, so the original's expressions are dead with it), and since DEF-189 a
// declaration's type and attributes, a `for` binding's type and an arm's pattern
// among them. The statement nodes themselves are left: nothing scans the
// statement array for meaning, and a dead one holds only blanks.
func:blank_stmt = NIL(Expander->:x, StmtId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        drop blank_stmt_window(x, raw stmt_list_start(s), raw stmt_list_count(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        drop blank_type(x, raw stmt_decl_type(s), f);
        int32:ac = raw stmt_decl_attr_count(x.ast, s);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...ac) {
            drop blank_attr(x, raw stmt_decl_attr(x.ast, s, ai), f);
        }
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_target(s), f);
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_assigned(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_while_invariant(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_while_measure(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        DeclId:fbid = raw stmt_for_binding(s);
        if (!(raw decl_is_none(fbid))) {
            drop blank_type(x, raw param_type(raw ast_decl(x.ast, fbid)), f);
        }
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_for_iter(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_for_invariant(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_for_measure(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_cond(s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_when_invariant(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_when_measure(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        int32:argc = raw stmt_counted_argc(x.ast, s);
        for (int32:i in 0i32...argc) {
            drop blank_tree(x, raw stmt_counted_arg(x.ast, s, i), f);
        }
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_invariant(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_measure(x.ast, s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw pick_selector(s), f);
        drop blank_stmt_window(x, raw pick_arm_start(s), raw pick_arm_count(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) {
        drop blank_pat(x, raw arm_pattern(s), f);
        drop blank_tree(x, raw arm_guard(s), f);
        drop blank_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s), f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        drop blank_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: s.a }, f);
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `break`, `continue` and `fall` carry a label; the rest carry one expression
    // in slot `a` -- the same list the clone ends with.
    bool:operand = raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt)   { operand = true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)   { operand = true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) { operand = true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)   { operand = true; }
    if (operand) { drop blank_tree(x, ExprId{ index: s.a }, f); }
    pass NIL;
};

func:blank_stmt_window = NIL(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        drop blank_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:blank_verify = NIL(Expander->:x, VerifyId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(x.ast, id);
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) { drop blank_tree(x, raw contract_cond(v), fuel); }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyJoinsWithin)  { drop blank_tree(x, raw contract_cond(v), fuel); }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyInvariantNode) {
        drop blank_window(x, raw invariant_start(v), raw invariant_count(v), fuel);
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyDecreasesNode) { drop blank_tree(x, raw measure_expr(v), fuel); }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE EXPRESSIONS INSIDE A DETACHED TYPE: every array size and every `comptime`
// argument, the suffix run followed in a loop as `expand_in_type` follows it. A
// type with no expression inside is the one the clone SHARED, and there is
// nothing in it to blank -- which is what makes this safe to call on any type of
// a detached original without asking which it was.
func:blank_type = NIL(Expander->:x, TypeId:start, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:f = fuel - 1i32;
    TypeId:cur = start;
    while (!(raw type_is_none(cur))) decreases cur.index {
        TypeNode:t = raw ast_type(x.ast, cur);
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeArrayType) {
            drop blank_tree(x, raw type_array_size(t), f);
            cur = raw type_element(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypePointerType)  { cur = raw type_pointee(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeOptionalType) { cur = raw type_inner(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeProjection)   { cur = raw type_projection_base(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeFuncType) {
            drop blank_type_window(x, raw type_param_start(t), raw type_param_count(t), f);
            cur = raw type_return(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeComptimeArg) {
            drop blank_tree(x, raw type_comptime_value(t), f);
            pass NIL;
        }
        if ((t.kind == TypeKind.TypeNamedType) || (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeDynType)) {
            drop blank_type_window(x, raw type_args_start(t), raw type_args_count(t), f);
            pass NIL;
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:blank_type_window = NIL(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count, int32:fuel) never fails {
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        drop blank_type(x, TypeId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) }, fuel);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A DETACHED PATTERN'S VALUE, OR ITS TWO BOUNDS. A destructure, the wildcard and
// `ERR:` hold no expression.
func:blank_pat = NIL(Expander->:x, PatId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw pat_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    PatNode:p = raw ast_pat(x.ast, id);
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatValue) { drop blank_tree(x, raw pat_value(p), fuel); }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatRange) {
        drop blank_tree(x, raw pat_range_lo(p), fuel);
        drop blank_tree(x, raw pat_range_hi(p), fuel);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A DETACHED ATTRIBUTE'S ARGUMENTS.
func:blank_attr = NIL(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:a = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (a.kind != DeclKind.DeclAttribute) { pass NIL; }
    drop blank_window(x, raw attr_arg_start(a), raw attr_arg_count(a), fuel);
    pass NIL;
};

// AN EXPRESSION-BODIED MACRO, SUBSTITUTED WHERE IT WAS INVOKED.
//
// Clone, copy the clone's ROOT over the invocation, then blank the clone's root.
// The children are shared rather than copied, so the only node written twice is
// the one being replaced and the only node left over is the clone's own root —
// which is blanked, so nothing is orphaned. Writing the clone directly into the
// invocation's slot would be one step shorter and would need the clone to know
// where its result was going, which is the coupling this avoids.
func:instantiate_expr = bool(Expander->:x, ExprId:id, ExprNode:inv, int32:decl) never fails {
    DeclNode:md = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: decl });
    if ((raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, md)) != (raw MACRO_BODY_EXPR())) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            "this macro's body is not a single expression, so it cannot stand where a value is expected",
            inv.span);
        pass false;
    }
    if (!(raw bind_invocation(x, md, inv, inv.span))) { pass false; }

    // THE BODY WINDOW HOLDS A `StmtId`, NOT AN `ExprId`. An expression body is one
    // EXPRESSION STATEMENT — that is how the parser recognises the shape — so the
    // expression is a step further in, and reading the window entry as an `ExprId`
    // clones whichever expression happens to sit at that index. It is the same
    // slot-means-two-things trap the builtin's generic count sprang, and it is
    // silent in exactly the same way: the wrong node is a real node, so the clone
    // succeeds and the program means something nobody wrote.
    StmtNode:bs = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, StmtId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, 0i32) });
    if (bs.kind != StmtKind.StmtExprStmt) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
            "this macro's body was classified as an expression but does not hold one",
            inv.span);
        pass false;
    }

    int32:saved_ps = x.params_start;   int32:saved_pc = x.params_count;
    int32:saved_as = x.args_start;     int32:saved_ac = x.args_count;
    bool:saved_site = x.at_decl_site;
    x.at_decl_site = false;
    drop record_site(x, md, inv.span);
    int64:hmark = raw ast_built_mark(x.ast);
    ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, ExprId{ index: bs.a }, raw CLONE_FUEL());
    x.params_start = saved_ps;  x.params_count = saved_pc;
    x.args_start = saved_as;    x.args_count = saved_ac;
    x.at_decl_site = saved_site;

    if (raw expr_is_none(c)) { pass false; }
    discard(raw ast_depth_pass(x.ast, hmark));
    if (raw splice_too_deep(x, raw ast_expr_height(x.ast, c), inv.span)) { pass false; }

    // THE INVOCATION'S OWN GENERIC ARGUMENTS are types nothing reads -- a macro
    // takes none (DEF-186), and they go with the invocation. What stands inside
    // one is blanked with it, as `blank_tree` does when the whole invocation is
    // detached (the statement and the splice forms), so the three positions
    // answer alike and none leaves an invocation for the audit to call a hole.
    drop blank_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(inv),
                           raw builtin_generic_count(inv), raw CLONE_FUEL());
    drop blank_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(inv)) + (raw builtin_generic_count(inv)),
                      (raw expr_list_count(inv)) - (raw builtin_generic_count(inv)),
                      raw CLONE_FUEL());

    // THE MARKS OF THE NODE BEING REPLACED AND OF THE CLONE'S ROOT MEET HERE, on
    // one node, and are composed into the one order the resolver applies (D-340;
    // `ast.npk`: the steps back, `HYG_SITE`, the roots). In the order they
    // happened: what the invocation's node already carried -- it may be an
    // argument's root, and it may be a root already, where an outer macro's body
    // was exactly this invocation -- then THIS expansion's root, then the clone's
    // root's own. A root followed by a step back is no move at all (the body is
    // exactly a parameter: `macro:id = (X) { X; };` leaves the argument standing
    // as though it had been written there), so those cancel in pairs; what is
    // left is steps, then roots.
    //
    // THE ROOTS ARE COUNTED. The mark was one bit, so an ALIAS -- a body that is
    // exactly an invocation, D-125 -- put two expansions on one node and the
    // resolver crossed one. That was the alias rule for `#caller` (the target's
    // escape reaches the alias's caller, and still does: `site_enter`), and it is
    // one site too few for an ARGUMENT: in `macro:w = (X) { #inner(X + k); };` the
    // `k` is `w`'s text and the `X` under it the caller's, two steps apart.
    //
    // AND THE ESCAPE COMES WITH THE CLONE'S ROOT, as it always did: a body of
    // exactly `#caller(name)` is a root and the escape at once, and the resolver
    // crosses the root before it reads the escape.
    int32:w1 = raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, id);
    int32:w2 = raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, c);
    int32:roots = (raw hyg_roots(w1)) + 1i32;
    int32:steps = raw hyg_back(w2);
    int32:cancel = steps;
    if (roots < cancel) { cancel = roots; }
    roots = (roots - cancel) + (raw hyg_roots(w2));
    steps = (raw hyg_back(w1)) + (steps - cancel);
    if (((w2 & (raw HYG_SITE())) != 0i32) && (roots > (raw hyg_roots(w2)))) {
        // A declaration macro's argument is module-level text: every expansion
        // between it and this node was stepped back out of, or the count is wrong.
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
            "a declaration macro's argument stands under an expansion its marks do not step out of; this is a defect in the expander, not a mistake in this program",
            inv.span);
        x.blown = true;
        pass false;
    }
    if ((roots > (raw HYG_COUNT_MAX())) || (steps > (raw HYG_COUNT_MAX()))) {
        if (!x.blown) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
                "this invocation stands under more nested expansions than expansion will follow (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
                inv.span);
        }
        x.blown = true;
        pass false;
    }

    ExprNode:cnode = raw ast_expr(x.ast, c);
    drop ast_replace_expr(x.ast, id, cnode);
    drop ast_set_expr_marks(x.ast, id, raw hyg_with(w1 | w2, steps, roots));
    drop ast_blank_expr(x.ast, c);
    pass true;
};

// A STATEMENT-BODIED MACRO BECOMES A BLOCK.
//
// NOT A RUN OF STATEMENTS SPLICED INTO THE CALLER'S BLOCK, and the block is what
// makes hygiene structural rather than a check. A `int32:tmp = …` in the body
// lives in the block's own scope: it cannot collide with a caller's `tmp`, it
// cannot leak out to be read after the invocation, and the block's PARENT is the
// module scope, so a free name in the body walks up to where the macro was written
// instead of into the caller's locals. One node buys the whole rule.
func:instantiate_stmt = bool(Expander->:x, StmtId:id, ExprId:inv_id,
                             ExprNode:inv, int32:decl, Span:at) never fails {
    DeclNode:md = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: decl });
    if (!(raw bind_invocation(x, md, inv, at))) { pass false; }

    int32:saved_ps = x.params_start;   int32:saved_pc = x.params_count;
    int32:saved_as = x.args_start;     int32:saved_ac = x.args_count;
    bool:saved_site = x.at_decl_site;
    x.at_decl_site = false;

    drop record_site(x, md, at);

    int32:bcount = raw macro_body_count(x.ast, md);
    int64:hmark = raw ast_built_mark(x.ast);
    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...bcount) {
        StmtId:cs = raw clone_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, i) },
                                     raw CLONE_FUEL());
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, cs.index);
    }
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);

    x.params_start = saved_ps;  x.params_count = saved_pc;
    x.args_start = saved_as;    x.args_count = saved_ac;
    x.at_decl_site = saved_site;

    // The statements land in a block that takes the invocation's place: the block
    // at the site's depth, the statements one below it.
    discard(raw ast_depth_pass(x.ast, hmark));
    int32:tallest = 0i32;
    for (int32:j in 0i32...w.count) {
        StmtId:ws = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, w.start, j) };
        if (!(raw stmt_is_none(ws))) {
            int32:hj = raw ast_stmt_height(x.ast, ws);
            if (hj > tallest) { tallest = hj; }
        }
    }
    if (raw splice_too_deep(x, tallest + 1i32, at)) { pass false; }

    // THE WHOLE INVOCATION, not just its arguments. Where an expression-position
    // expansion is written OVER the invocation's own node, this one replaces the
    // STATEMENT — so the invocation expression is left behind, pointed at by
    // nothing, and the audit would find it standing there and refuse a program
    // that had expanded correctly.
    //
    // AND WHAT THE INVOCATION'S NODE CARRIED GOES TO THE BLOCK (D-340). The
    // invocation may be an argument's root -- `macro:both = (X) { X; X; };` over
    // `#both(#set(n))` leaves two statements that are each the caller's text --
    // and it may be a root already (an expression macro whose body is exactly
    // this invocation). The block is where that node's place in the program now
    // is, so it takes the steps back, `HYG_SITE` and the roots, and adds its own.
    int32:iw = raw ast_expr_marks(x.ast, inv_id);
    if ((raw hyg_roots(iw)) >= (raw HYG_COUNT_MAX())) {
        if (!x.blown) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
                "this invocation stands under more nested expansions than expansion will follow (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
                at);
        }
        x.blown = true;
        pass false;
    }
    drop blank_tree(x, inv_id, raw CLONE_FUEL());

    StmtNode:blk = StmtNode{ kind: StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt, span: at,
                             a: 0i32, b: w.start, c: w.count, payload: 0i64 };
    drop ast_replace_stmt(x.ast, id, blk);
    int32:sw = (raw ast_stmt_marks(x.ast, id)) | (iw & (raw HYG_SITE()));
    drop ast_set_stmt_marks(x.ast, id, raw hyg_with(sw, raw hyg_back(iw), (raw hyg_roots(iw)) + 1i32));
    pass true;
};

// THE WALK THAT FINDS THEM. Per MODULE rather than over the whole array, because
// a macro is invocable only where it was declared (D-124) and an array scan cannot
// say which module a node is in.
//
// A WALK CAN HAVE A HOLE — a statement kind nobody added a case for, whose
// contents are then never visited. That is the failure this compiler has paid for
// four times, so the walk is not trusted on its own: `expand_audit` scans the
// whole expression array afterwards and refuses any invocation that is still
// standing. The walk is the mechanism and the scan is the proof, and a hole in the
// first shows up as a refusal rather than as a program that quietly did nothing.

// THE DEPTH OF THE WALK is kept by these two wrappers and nowhere else: each level
// of the tree passes through exactly one of them, as it passes through one
// constructor when it is built, so `x.depth` is the tree depth the heights measure.
func:expand_in_expr = bool(Expander->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    x.depth = x.depth + 1i32;
    bool:r = raw expand_in_expr_node(x, id);
    x.depth = x.depth - 1i32;
    pass r;
};

func:expand_in_stmt = bool(Expander->:x, StmtId:id) never fails {
    x.depth = x.depth + 1i32;
    bool:r = raw expand_in_stmt_node(x, id);
    x.depth = x.depth - 1i32;
    pass r;
};

// A SPLICE MAY NOT NEST PAST THE BOUND (DEF-150's c2): its clone lands at the site's
// depth, and the parser measured the macro's body and the site's tree apart, so the
// sum is measured here -- the site's depth plus the placed subtree's height, less
// the one level they share. Refused once, as the clone's own fuel is.
func:splice_too_deep = bool(Expander->:x, int32:placed, Span:at) never fails {
    if ((x.depth + placed - 1i32) <= (raw AST_DEPTH_MAX())) { pass false; }
    if (!x.blown) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
            "this expansion nests deeper than 256 levels where it lands; split the macro's body or the expression around the invocation into named parts (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
            at);
    }
    x.blown = true;
    pass true;
};

func:expand_in_expr_node = bool(Expander->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprNone) { pass false; }
    drop ast_set_expr_flag(x.ast, id, raw HYG_SEEN());

    int32:decl = raw macro_here(x, n);
    if (decl >= 0i32) {
        if (raw probe_standing(x, id)) { pass false; }
        pass (raw instantiate_expr(x, id, n, decl));
    }

    int32:shape = raw expr_shape(n.kind);
    bool:hit = false;

    // THE TYPES AN EXPRESSION CARRIES ARE WALKED TOO (DEF-170): a turbofish's and
    // a builtin's generic arguments at the front of the window, and a cast's
    // target. `list_init::<int32[#n()]>(…)`, `#size_of<int32[#n()]>()` and
    // `p =>! int32[#n()]->` each hold an array size the walk never reached.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                        raw expr_generic_count(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_callee(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw expr_generic_count(n)),
                                   (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw expr_generic_count(n)))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                        raw builtin_generic_count(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_window(x, (raw expr_list_start(n)) + (raw builtin_generic_count(n)),
                                   (raw expr_list_count(n)) - (raw builtin_generic_count(n)))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw expr_cast_type(n))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    // A `dyn` cast holds its target's trait window directly (parse_expr.npk).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDynCastExpr) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_operand(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                        raw expr_list_count(n))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:cnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
        int32:i = 1i32;
        while (i < cnt) decreases cnt - i {
            if (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast,
                                       raw expr_list_start(n), i) })) { hit = true; }
            i = i + 2i32;
        }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw pickx_selector(n))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt_window(x, raw pickx_arm_start(n),
                                        raw pickx_arm_count(n))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }

    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LEAF())) { pass false; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_NONE())) { pass false; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_LIST())) {
        pass (raw expand_in_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n), raw expr_list_count(n)));
    }
    if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_lhs(n))) { hit = true; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONE())) { pass hit; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_ONELIST())) {
        if (raw expand_in_window(x, raw expr_list_start(n),
                                   raw expr_list_count(n))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_rhs(n))) { hit = true; }
    if (shape == (raw EXPR_SHAPE_THREE())) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw expr_third(n))) { hit = true; }
    }
    pass hit;
};

func:expand_in_window = bool(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) })) {
            hit = true;
        }
    }
    pass hit;
};

func:expand_in_stmt_window = bool(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) })) {
            hit = true;
        }
    }
    pass hit;
};

func:expand_in_stmt_node = bool(Expander->:x, StmtId:id) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, id);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtNone) { pass false; }

    // A BARE INVOCATION AS A STATEMENT. Only `StmtExprStmt` — `discard(#m())` and
    // `prove(#m())` carry an expression too, but what stands there is a VALUE, so
    // an expression-bodied macro belongs to the expression walk below and a
    // statement-bodied one does not fit at all.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExprStmt) {
        ExprId:ex = ExprId{ index: s.a };
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(ex))) {
            ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ex);
            int32:decl = raw macro_here(x, n);
            if (decl >= 0i32) {
                if (raw probe_standing(x, ex)) { pass false; }
                DeclNode:md = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: decl });
                int32:bk = raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, md);
                if (bk == (raw MACRO_BODY_STMTS())) {
                    pass (raw instantiate_stmt(x, id, ex, n, decl, s.span));
                }
                if (bk == (raw MACRO_BODY_DECLS())) {
                    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
                        "this macro's body is declarations, and a declaration cannot stand inside a function body",
                        s.span);
                    pass false;
                }
                // An expression body: fall through, and the expression walk
                // substitutes it in place as it would anywhere else.
            }
        }
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        pass (raw expand_in_stmt_window(x, raw stmt_list_start(s),
                                          raw stmt_list_count(s)));
    }
    // EVERY EXPRESSION A STATEMENT CARRIES (DEF-170, 1.6.1e step 3; the library
    // listener's mc0278). Until this step the arms below followed the condition
    // and the body and nothing else, so an invocation in a loop's `decreases` or
    // `invariant`, in a declaration's type or attribute, or in an arm's pattern
    // was never expanded and the audit refused it as a hole in this walk -- eight
    // positions measured, each MACRO-006 in a correct program. The children are
    // the clone's own, kind by kind (`clone_stmt`), so the two cannot disagree
    // about what a statement holds.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw stmt_decl_type(s))) { hit = true; }
        int32:ac = raw stmt_decl_attr_count(x.ast, s);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...ac) {
            if (raw expand_in_attr(x, raw stmt_decl_attr(x.ast, s, ai))) { hit = true; }
        }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_target(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_assigned(s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_then(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_else(s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_while_invariant(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_while_measure(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_body(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        // The binding is a parameter declaration: its type is what it carries.
        if (raw expand_in_param(x, raw stmt_for_binding(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_for_iter(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_for_invariant(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_for_measure(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_for_body(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_cond(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_when_invariant(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_when_measure(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_body(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_then(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_when_end(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) { pass (raw expand_in_counted(x, s)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt) { pass (raw expand_in_counted(x, s)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw pick_selector(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt_window(x, raw pick_arm_start(s),
                                        raw pick_arm_count(s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickArm) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_pat(x, raw arm_pattern(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw arm_guard(s))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw arm_body(s))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        pass (raw expand_in_stmt(x, StmtId{ index: s.a }));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)    { pass false; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) { pass false; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt)     { pass false; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt)   { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a })); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)   { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a })); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a })); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)   { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a })); }
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind))     { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, ExprId{ index: s.a })); }

    drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(),
        "this statement kind has no entry in the expansion walk, so an invocation written inside one would never be found",
        s.span);
    x.blown = true;
    pass false;
};

func:expand_in_counted = bool(Expander->:x, StmtNode:s) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    int32:argc = raw stmt_counted_argc(x.ast, s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...argc) {
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw stmt_counted_arg(x.ast, s, i))) { hit = true; }
    }
    if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_invariant(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
    if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw stmt_counted_measure(x.ast, s))) { hit = true; }
    if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw stmt_counted_body(s))) { hit = true; }
    pass hit;
};

// --- the positions that are not a statement's own slots (DEF-170) -----------------
//
// A VERIFICATION NODE'S EXPRESSIONS: a contract's or a `joins` clause's one, an
// invariant's window, a measure's one (none under `unbounded`). A `limit` names a
// `Rules` block and the three markers carry nothing. NO DEPTH RESET: the clone
// hands these the fuel of the statement that carries them and `ast_depth.npk`
// counts them at that statement's own level, so the walk's depth does the same.
func:expand_in_verify = bool(Expander->:x, VerifyId:id) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(x.ast, id);
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) {
        pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw contract_cond(v)));
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyJoinsWithin) {
        pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw contract_cond(v)));
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyInvariantNode) {
        pass (raw expand_in_window(x, raw invariant_start(v), raw invariant_count(v)));
    }
    if (v.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyDecreasesNode) {
        pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw measure_expr(v)));
    }
    pass false;
};

// AN EXPRESSION THAT IS ITS OWN ROOT: an array size, a `comptime` argument, a
// pattern's value, an attribute's argument. The parser measured each as a tree of
// its own -- `ast_depth.npk` follows none of them from the node that carries them
// -- so the walk's depth restarts, and a splice there is held to the bound from
// the expression itself, as the parser held what was written there.
func:expand_root_expr = bool(Expander->:x, ExprId:id) never fails {
    int32:saved = x.depth;
    x.depth = 0i32;
    bool:r = raw expand_in_expr(x, id);
    x.depth = saved;
    pass r;
};

// THE EXPRESSIONS INSIDE A TYPE: an array's size and a `comptime` argument
// (`int32[#n()]`, `Mutex<Config, #lvl()>`), wherever the type stands -- a
// binding, a parameter, a field, a return type, a cast's target, a generic
// argument, a pointee.
//
// SUBSTITUTED IN PLACE, EACH INSTANTIATION'S OWN. A type that holds an expression
// is cloned with the body that wrote it (`clone_type`, DEF-189), so an invocation
// inside one reaches the walk as that instantiation's clone and is substituted
// there, for it alone. (From DEF-170 until DEF-189 the type was the template's
// node, shared, and its invocation was substituted once for every instantiation.)
//
// `->`, `?`, `[N]` and `.Item` EACH WRAP ONE TYPE and the parser builds a run of
// them in a loop (`p_suffixes`), so the run is followed in a loop here: a frame
// per suffix would make this the first walk to run out of stack on a type the
// parser read without recursing. A type node is built after the type it wraps,
// which is why the index falls along the run.
func:expand_in_type = bool(Expander->:x, TypeId:start) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    TypeId:cur = start;
    while (!(raw type_is_none(cur))) decreases cur.index {
        TypeNode:t = raw ast_type(x.ast, cur);
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeArrayType) {
            if (raw expand_root_expr(x, raw type_array_size(t))) { hit = true; }
            cur = raw type_element(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypePointerType)  { cur = raw type_pointee(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeOptionalType) { cur = raw type_inner(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeProjection)   { cur = raw type_projection_base(t); continue; }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeFuncType) {
            if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw type_param_start(t),
                                            raw type_param_count(t))) { hit = true; }
            cur = raw type_return(t);
            continue;
        }
        if (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeComptimeArg) {
            if (raw expand_root_expr(x, raw type_comptime_value(t))) { hit = true; }
            pass hit;
        }
        // A named type's arguments and a `dyn`'s traits are both a window of
        // types in `a`, `b`.
        if ((t.kind == TypeKind.TypeNamedType) || (t.kind == TypeKind.TypeDynType)) {
            if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw type_args_start(t),
                                            raw type_args_count(t))) { hit = true; }
            pass hit;
        }
        // `cstring`, `any` and `Self` hold nothing.
        pass hit;
    }
    pass hit;
};

func:expand_in_type_window = bool(Expander->:x, int32:start, int32:count) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...count) {
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, TypeId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast, start, i) })) {
            hit = true;
        }
    }
    pass hit;
};

// A PATTERN'S VALUE AND A RANGE PATTERN'S TWO BOUNDS, substituted in place -- in
// the program's own patterns, and in each instantiation's clone of a body's
// (`clone_pat`). A struct destructure names a type that takes no arguments by its
// grammar, an enum destructure names segments and bindings, and the wildcard and
// `ERR:` carry nothing.
//
// THE PATTERN'S KIND IS THE PARSER'S AND DOES NOT CHANGE. `(1i32..5i32)` is a
// RANGE pattern because the parser saw the `..` and put the two bounds on the
// pattern; `(#m())` is a VALUE pattern, read before anybody knows what `m` is. So
// a macro whose body is a range cannot stand as a whole pattern: it would leave a
// range VALUE where one value is matched, which no later stage reads as a range
// pattern (the checker types no pattern for its own sake, and the emitter met it
// as a construct it cannot lower). Refused here, at the pattern, as a body that
// does not fit where it landed; the range is written in the pattern and its
// bounds expanded -- `(#lo()..#hi())`.
func:expand_in_pat = bool(Expander->:x, PatId:id) never fails {
    if (raw pat_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    PatNode:p = raw ast_pat(x.ast, id);
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatValue) {
        bool:vhit = raw expand_root_expr(x, raw pat_value(p));
        ExprNode:now = raw ast_expr(x.ast, raw pat_value(p));
        if (now.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
                "this is a value pattern, and the macro it invokes expands to a range: a pattern's kind is read where it is written, so an expansion cannot make it a range pattern; write the range in the pattern and expand its bounds -- `(#lo()..#hi())`",
                p.span);
        }
        pass vhit;
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatRange) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_root_expr(x, raw pat_range_lo(p))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_root_expr(x, raw pat_range_hi(p))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    pass false;
};

// AN ATTRIBUTE'S ARGUMENTS -- `#[align(#n())]` -- on whatever carries it.
func:expand_in_attr = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:a = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (a.kind != DeclKind.DeclAttribute) { pass false; }
    bool:hit = false;
    int32:n = raw attr_arg_count(a);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        if (raw expand_root_expr(x, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast,
                                  raw attr_arg_start(a), i) })) { hit = true; }
    }
    pass hit;
};

// A PARAMETER -- a function's, an extern function's, or a `for` binding -- and a
// variadic tail: the type is what each carries (a `limit` names a rule).
func:expand_in_param = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:p = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (p.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl)    { pass (raw expand_in_type(x, raw param_type(p))); }
    if (p.kind == DeclKind.DeclVariadicSpec) { pass (raw expand_in_type(x, raw variadic_type(p))); }
    pass false;
};

// A GENERIC PARAMETER: a `comptime` one has a value type, a type one a window of
// bounds, and each is a type that may hold a size or a value argument.
func:expand_in_generic = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:g = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (g.kind != DeclKind.DeclGenericParam) { pass false; }
    bool:hit = false;
    if (raw generic_is_value(g)) {
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw generic_value_type(g))) { hit = true; }
    }
    if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw generic_bound_start(g),
                                    raw generic_bound_count(g))) { hit = true; }
    pass hit;
};

// THE BODIES A DECLARATION OWNS. Not the macro declarations themselves: a body
// expands when it is INSTANTIATED, and expanding it in place would substitute the
// inner macro's parameters against nothing and leave the outer's unbound.
//
// AND EVERY EXPRESSION A DECLARATION CARRIES OUTSIDE A BODY (DEF-170, 1.6.1e step
// 3): a function's signature types, contracts and attributes, a global's type, a
// field's, a variant's value and payload types, a `Rules` block's subject and
// clauses, a unit's right-hand side, an error's code, an item's generic bounds and
// attributes, an impl's target and trait. Each was a position the audit refused
// as a hole in this walk (`Rules`, `requires`, `ensures` and a function's
// `decreases` among the eight the step measured; the rest found by placing an
// invocation in every position the parser reads an expression at).
func:expand_in_decl = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);

    // A macro's BODY is a template and is not walked; the attributes written on
    // the declaration are program text.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroDecl) {
        bool:hit = false;
        int32:mac = raw macro_attr_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:mi in 0i32...mac) {
            if (raw expand_in_attr(x, raw macro_attr(x.ast, d, mi))) { hit = true; }
        }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl)  { pass false; }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) { pass false; }

    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) {
        bool:hit = false;
        int32:gc = raw fn_generic_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:gi in 0i32...gc) {
            if (raw expand_in_generic(x, raw fn_generic(x.ast, d, gi))) { hit = true; }
        }
        int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:pi in 0i32...pc) {
            if (raw expand_in_param(x, raw fn_param(x.ast, d, pi))) { hit = true; }
        }
        if (raw expand_in_param(x, raw fn_variadic(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw fn_return(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        // A contract's predicate hangs from the declaration, as a module-level
        // initialiser does: its own first level.
        int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:ci in 0i32...cc) {
            if (raw expand_in_verify(x, raw fn_contract(x.ast, d, ci))) { hit = true; }
        }
        int32:ac = raw fn_attr_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...ac) {
            if (raw expand_in_attr(x, raw fn_attr(x.ast, d, ai))) { hit = true; }
        }
        if (raw expand_in_stmt(x, raw fn_body(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclGlobalDecl) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw global_type(d))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw global_init(d))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl) {
        pass (raw expand_in_type(x, raw field_type(d)));
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumVariant) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_root_expr(x, raw variant_value(d))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_type_window(x, raw variant_payload_start(d),
                                        raw variant_payload_count(d))) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclRuleDecl) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw rule_subject(d))) { hit = true; }
        int32:cn = raw rule_clause_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:ci in 0i32...cn) {
            if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw rule_clause(x.ast, d, ci))) { hit = true; }
        }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclUnitDecl)      { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw unit_rhs(d))); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclErrorDecl)     { pass (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw errdecl_code(d))); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclAssocTypeDecl) { pass (raw expand_in_type(x, raw assoc_default(d))); }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclExternFn) {
        bool:hit = false;
        int32:pc = raw extern_fn_param_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:pi in 0i32...pc) {
            if (raw expand_in_param(x, raw extern_fn_param(x.ast, d, pi))) { hit = true; }
        }
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw extern_fn_return(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        DeclId:fail_id = raw extern_fn_failure(x.ast, d);
        if (!(raw decl_is_none(fail_id))) {
            DeclNode:fail_node = raw ast_decl(x.ast, fail_id);
            if (fail_node.kind == DeclKind.DeclFailsOn) {
                if (raw expand_in_expr(x, raw failson_predicate(fail_node))) { hit = true; }
            }
        }
        pass hit;
    }
    // THE THREE ITEM SITES. A splice among their members is instantiated INTO the
    // member list, which is the thing D-057 kept `macro:` alive for — generics,
    // `comptime` and `#[derive]` can none of them add a field to a struct or a
    // method to an impl.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclStructDecl) {
        bool:hit = raw expand_item_head(x, d);
        if (raw expand_item_window(x, id, raw SITE_STRUCT())) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumDecl) {
        bool:hit = raw expand_item_head(x, d);
        if (raw expand_item_window(x, id, raw SITE_ENUM())) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl) {
        bool:hit = raw expand_item_head(x, d);
        if (raw expand_item_window(x, id, raw SITE_IMPL())) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }

    // AN `impl` HAS A LAYOUT OF ITS OWN and is not an "item". Its header is five
    // slots — target, trait, member count, attribute count, generic count — where
    // an item's is four, so `item_member_count` on one reads the TRAIT'S TYPE ID as
    // a member count and walks that many slots of whatever follows.
    //
    // The symptom was not a wrong answer. It was a segmentation fault in files with
    // no macro in them at all, dependent on how big the rest of the program
    // happened to be, because the count read was a type index that could be
    // anything. `impl_member_count` and `impl_member` are the accessors, and they
    // exist for exactly this reason.
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) {
        bool:hit = false;
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw impl_target(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw impl_trait(x.ast, d))) { hit = true; }
        int32:gc = raw impl_generic_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:gi in 0i32...gc) {
            if (raw expand_in_generic(x, raw impl_generic(x.ast, d, gi))) { hit = true; }
        }
        int32:ac = raw impl_attr_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...ac) {
            if (raw expand_in_attr(x, raw impl_attr(x.ast, d, ai))) { hit = true; }
        }
        if (raw expand_impl_window(x, id)) { hit = true; }
        pass hit;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclExternBlock) {
        bool:hit = false;
        int32:n = raw decl_win_count(d);
        for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
            if (raw expand_in_decl(x, DeclId{ index: raw ast_id_at(x.ast,
                                     raw decl_win_start(d), i) })) { hit = true; }
        }
        pass hit;
    }
    // An import, an `opaque struct` and the `never fails` of an extern function
    // carry no expression. A kind this does not name is not walked, and the audit
    // is what says so: an invocation written in one arrives there as a hole.
    pass false;
};

// WHAT AN ITEM CARRIES BESIDE ITS MEMBERS: the generic parameters' bounds, the
// attributes, and a trait's supertraits (the fourth list, empty for the rest).
// The members are `expand_item_window`'s, which rebuilds the list when a splice
// stands in it; none of these three moves.
func:expand_item_head = bool(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d) never fails {
    bool:hit = false;
    int32:gc = raw item_generic_count(x.ast, d);
    for (int32:gi in 0i32...gc) {
        if (raw expand_in_generic(x, raw item_generic(x.ast, d, gi))) { hit = true; }
    }
    int32:ac = raw item_attr_count(x.ast, d);
    for (int32:ai in 0i32...ac) {
        if (raw expand_in_attr(x, raw item_attr(x.ast, d, ai))) { hit = true; }
    }
    int32:ec = raw item_extra_count(x.ast, d);
    for (int32:ei in 0i32...ec) {
        if (raw expand_in_type(x, raw item_extra(x.ast, d, ei))) { hit = true; }
    }
    pass hit;
};

// A MEMBER LIST WITH SPLICES IN IT, REBUILT. The same shape as the module's, and
// the same reason for the scan first: a window rebuilt every round when nothing
// changed would churn the pool for every struct in the program.
//
// AN `impl` IS NOT AN ITEM — five header slots against four, in a different order —
// so it gets its own, below. That distinction cost a day in 0.6.2 and is stated at
// every place it matters rather than once.
func:expand_item_window = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:site) never fails {
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    int32:gc = raw item_generic_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:mc = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ac = raw item_attr_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ec = raw item_extra_count(x.ast, d);

    bool:found = false;
    for (int32:scan in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclNode:sm = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, d, scan));
        if (sm.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) { found = true; }
    }
    if (!found) {
        // Still descend: a method body may hold an invocation of its own.
        bool:hit = false;
        for (int32:k in 0i32...mc) {
            if (raw expand_in_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d, k))) { hit = true; }
        }
        pass hit;
    }

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, 0i32);      // member count -- patched below
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ec);

    for (int32:g in 0i32...gc) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_generic(x.ast, d, g)).index);
    }

    int32:emitted = 0i32;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclId:mid = raw item_member(x.ast, d, i);
        DeclNode:mn = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mid);
        if (mn.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) {
            emitted = emitted + (raw expand_splice(x, mn, site));
        } else {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, mid.index);
            emitted = emitted + 1i32;
        }
    }

    for (int32:a2 in 0i32...ac) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_attr(x.ast, d, a2)).index);
    }
    for (int32:e2 in 0i32...ec) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_extra(x.ast, d, e2)).index);
    }

    drop ast_scratch_set(x.ast, mark, 1i32, emitted);
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    drop ast_set_decl_window(x.ast, id, w.start, w.count);

    DeclNode:d2 = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    int32:n2 = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d2);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...n2) {
        discard(raw expand_in_decl(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d2, j)));
    }
    pass true;
};

func:expand_impl_window = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:id) never fails {
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    int32:gc = raw impl_generic_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:mc = raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d);
    int32:ac = raw impl_attr_count(x.ast, d);

    bool:found = false;
    for (int32:scan in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclNode:sm = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, scan));
        if (sm.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) { found = true; }
    }
    if (!found) {
        bool:hit = false;
        for (int32:k in 0i32...mc) {
            if (raw expand_in_decl(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, k))) { hit = true; }
        }
        pass hit;
    }

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw impl_target(x.ast, d)).index);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw impl_trait(x.ast, d)).index);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, 0i32);      // member count -- patched below
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);

    for (int32:g in 0i32...gc) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw impl_generic(x.ast, d, g)).index);
    }

    int32:emitted = 0i32;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclId:mid = raw impl_member(x.ast, d, i);
        DeclNode:mn = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mid);
        if (mn.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) {
            emitted = emitted + (raw expand_splice(x, mn, raw SITE_IMPL()));
        } else {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, mid.index);
            emitted = emitted + 1i32;
        }
    }

    for (int32:a2 in 0i32...ac) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw impl_attr(x.ast, d, a2)).index);
    }

    drop ast_scratch_set(x.ast, mark, 2i32, emitted);
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    drop ast_set_decl_window(x.ast, id, w.start, w.count);

    DeclNode:d2 = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    int32:n2 = raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d2);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...n2) {
        discard(raw expand_in_decl(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d2, j)));
    }
    pass true;
};

// --- the audit ------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// EVERY `#name(...)` LEFT STANDING IS ONE OF TWO THINGS, and neither may pass. It
// is a compiler builtin — `#size_of`, `#wild_ptr`, `#wild_slice` — or it is a
// macro that does not exist here, and until this ran the second was accepted in
// silence: `#totally_not_a_macro(3i32)` typed as INVALID, and the invalid type is
// how the checker suppresses cascades, so it produced no diagnostic at all.
//
// A WHOLE-ARRAY SCAN, deliberately. It is the counterpart to the walk above and it
// is checking the walk as much as the program: an invocation the walk never
// reached is still in the array, so a hole in the walk arrives here as a refusal
// naming the invocation rather than as a program that silently did nothing.
pub func:expand_audit = NIL(Expander->:x) never fails {
    int32:i = 1i32;
    int32:nexprs = raw ast_expr_count(x.ast);
    while (i < nexprs) decreases nexprs - i {
        ExprId:id = ExprId{ index: i };
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, id);
        // A MACRO BODY IS A TEMPLATE, not program text. `#caller(x)` there is
        // consumed by the CLONE, and a nested `#inner()` expands into the caller
        // rather than where it is written, so neither is standing anywhere it
        // should be refused.
        //
        // AND NO INSTANTIATION LEADS THE WALK INTO ONE (DEF-189). Every expression
        // a body holds is cloned -- the ones inside its types, patterns,
        // attributes and generic parameters with the rest -- so what the walk
        // reaches through an instantiation is the clone, which carries no mark and
        // is audited like any program text: `(#no_such())` as a pattern in an
        // instantiated body is refused at the clone, at the span the body wrote.
        // (From DEF-170 until DEF-189 those four were the template's own nodes,
        // shared by every instantiation, and a marked expression the walk had
        // SEEN was audited here for that reason.)
        if (raw ast_expr_flag(x.ast, id, raw HYG_IN_MACRO())) {
            i = i + 1i32;
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
            int32:name = raw builtin_name(n);
            string:t = raw intern_get(x.interns, name);
            if (raw string_eq(t, "caller")) {
                drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_CALLER_FORM(),
                    "`#caller` is legal only inside a macro body, where it names something at the invocation site; outside one there is no invocation to reach",
                    n.span);
            } else {
                if (!(raw is_hash_builtin(t))) {
                    // NEVER VISITED IS A DEFECT IN THE COMPILER, not in the
                    // program. The walk goes everywhere an invocation can stand;
                    // an invocation it never entered means a construct it has no
                    // case for, and the reader has nothing to change.
                    if (!(raw ast_expr_flag(x.ast, id, raw HYG_SEEN()))) {
                        string:w1 = string_concat("`#", t);
                        string:w2 = string_concat(w1,
                            "` stands somewhere macro expansion never walks, so it was never expanded; this is a hole in the expander, not a mistake in this program");
                        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_INTERNAL(), move(w2), n.span);
                    } else {
                    if (raw macrotable_find_elsewhere(@x.macros, name)) {
                        // Declared, but not here. The macro is real and the
                        // invocation is not reaching it.
                        string:l1 = string_concat("`#", t);
                        string:l2 = string_concat(l1,
                            "` is declared in another module, and a macro is invocable only in the module that declares it");
                        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_NOT_LOCAL(), move(l2), n.span);
                    } else {
                        string:m1 = string_concat("`#", t);
                        string:m2 = string_concat(m1,
                            "` names no macro and no compiler builtin; `#` is how both are spelled, so check the name against the macro's declaration");
                        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_UNKNOWN(), move(m2), n.span);
                    }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1i32;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE LINE RANGE A MACRO'S BODY OCCUPIES, computed from its items' spans.
//
// The declaration's own span covers its head, not its body — so the range is the
// minimum and maximum line over the body's members, whichever node kind they are.
// A body of one expression is one line; a body of declarations is as many as it
// takes.
func:record_site = NIL(Expander->:x, DeclNode:md, Span:site) never fails {
    int32:n = raw macro_body_count(x.ast, md);
    if (n <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }

    int32:kind = raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, md);
    int32:file = md.span.file;
    int32:lo = 0i32;
    int32:hi = 0i32;
    bool:first = true;

    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        int32:idx = raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, i);
        Span:sp = md.span;
        if (kind == (raw MACRO_BODY_DECLS())) {
            sp = (raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: idx })).span;
        } else {
            sp = (raw ast_stmt(x.ast, StmtId{ index: idx })).span;
        }
        if (first) { lo = sp.line; hi = sp.line; file = sp.file; first = false; }
        if (sp.line < lo) { lo = sp.line; }
        if (sp.line > hi) { hi = sp.line; }
    }

    // THE CLOSING BRACE IS NOT A MEMBER, so a diagnostic on the body's last line
    // could sit one past the last item's start line. One line of slack rather than
    // a parse of the body's extent, which the AST does not record.
    MacroSite:e = MacroSite{ file: file, lo: lo, hi: hi + 1i32, site: site };
    drop sitetable_add(@x.sites, e);
    pass NIL;
};

// A DIAGNOSTIC INSIDE AN EXPANDED BODY GETS TOLD WHERE IT WAS EXPANDED.
//
// Run once, just before reporting, because a diagnostic about expanded code can
// come from ANY later stage — the resolver, the type checker, an analysis — and
// each of them knows nothing about macros. Adding the note where the diagnostic is
// created would mean teaching every one of them; adding it here means teaching
// none.
//
// THE ORIGINAL COUNT IS TAKEN FIRST, because the notes are pushed onto the same
// list being scanned.
//
// A NOTE IS NEVER ANNOTATED (DEF-173, 1.6.1e step 3). A note sits at an
// INVOCATION, and an invocation one line below a one-line body lies inside that
// body's range by the line of slack `record_site` allows -- so a second pass over
// the list annotated the first pass's note with "the NITPICK-MACRO-009 at line 3
// lies in a macro body", about a line that is not in one. The driver made that
// second pass at four of its returns (two calls in a row since 0.7.8 moved the
// pipeline out of `tools/check.npk`, where each return had one); it calls once
// now, and a note is skipped here whoever calls.
pub func:expansion_notes = NIL(Expander->:x, DiagList->:d) never fails {
    int64:n = raw diaglist_count(d);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) {
        Diagnostic:g = raw diaglist_at(d, i);
        if (g.severity == 0i32) { continue; }
        int64:s = 0i64;
        while (s < x.sites.v.count) decreases x.sites.v.count - s {
            MacroSite:e = x.sites.v[s];
            bool:inside = (g.span.file == e.file);
            if (inside) { inside = (g.span.line >= e.lo); }
            if (inside) { inside = (g.span.line <= e.hi); }
            if (inside) {
                // THE NOTE NAMES THE DIAGNOSTIC IT ANNOTATES (1.0.8): it sits
                // at the INVOCATION, which is not "inside a macro body", and
                // after sorting it may be far from the line it explains — so
                // the line is in the sentence.
                string:n1 = string_concat("the ", g.code);
                string:n2 = string_concat(n1, " at line ");
                string:n3 = string_concat(n2,
                                int_to_string(g.span.line => int64));
                drop diaglist_push(d, raw diag_note(raw MACRO_EXPANDED_HERE(),
                    string_concat(n3,
                        " lies in a macro body that this invocation expanded"),
                    e.site));
            }
            s = s + 1i64;
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the fixed-point loop ---------------------------------------------------------

pub func:expander_init = Expander(Ast->:ast, InternTable->:interns,
                                  DiagList->:diags) never fails {
    Expander:x = Expander{ ast: ast, interns: interns, diags: diags,
                           macros: raw macrotable_init(),
                           sites: raw sitetable_init(),
                           params_start: 0i32, params_count: 0i32,
                           args_start: 0i32, args_count: 0i32,
                           cur_module: 0i32, blown: false, depth: 0i32,
                           probing: false, standing: 0i32,
                           in_arg: 0i32, at_decl_site: false, mod_depth: 0i32 };
    pass x;
};

// Every `macro:` declaration in a module, into the table. Collection precedes
// expansion for the same reason the resolver collects before it binds: an
// invocation may name a macro declared after it.
pub func:collect_macros = NIL(Expander->:x, DeclId:mod_id) never fails {
    DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mod_id);
    int32:n = raw item_member_count(x.ast, m);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        DeclId:id = raw item_member(x.ast, m, i);
        DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
        if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroDecl) {
            drop macrotable_add(@x.macros, raw decl_name(d), id.index, mod_id.index);
        }
        if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
            drop collect_macros(x, id);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// ONE ROUND over a module's members. Returns whether anything expanded, which is
// what tells the loop whether to come back.
pub func:expand_module = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:mod_id) never fails {
    int32:saved_module = x.cur_module;
    x.cur_module = mod_id.index;
    bool:r = raw expand_module_here(x, mod_id);
    x.cur_module = saved_module;
    pass r;
};

func:expand_module_here = bool(Expander->:x, DeclId:mod_id) never fails {
    DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mod_id);
    int32:gc = raw item_generic_count(x.ast, m);
    int32:mc = raw item_member_count(x.ast, m);
    int32:ac = raw item_attr_count(x.ast, m);
    int32:ec = raw item_extra_count(x.ast, m);

    // NOTHING TO DO IS THE COMMON CASE, and rebuilding a window that did not change
    // would churn the pool on every round of every module.
    bool:found_splice = false;
    for (int32:scan in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclNode:s = raw ast_decl(x.ast, raw item_member(x.ast, m, scan));
        if (s.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) { found_splice = true; }
    }
    if (!found_splice) {
        // NO SPLICE AMONG THE MEMBERS IS NOT NOTHING TO DO. An invocation also
        // stands as a statement and as an expression, so every member's body is
        // walked whether or not the member list itself changed — and a nested
        // module may have a splice of its own.
        bool:nested = false;
        for (int32:k in 0i32...mc) {
            DeclId:id = raw item_member(x.ast, m, k);
            DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
            if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
                if (raw expand_module(x, id)) { nested = true; }
            } else {
                if (raw expand_in_decl(x, id)) { nested = true; }
            }
        }
        pass nested;
    }

    int32:mark = raw ast_scratch_mark(x.ast);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, gc);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, 0i32);      // member count — patched below
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ac);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, ec);

    for (int32:g in 0i32...gc) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_generic(x.ast, m, g)).index);
    }

    int32:emitted = 0i32;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...mc) {
        DeclId:id = raw item_member(x.ast, m, i);
        DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
        if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice) {
            emitted = emitted + (raw expand_splice(x, d, raw SITE_MODULE()));
        } else {
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, id.index);
            emitted = emitted + 1i32;
        }
    }

    for (int32:a2 in 0i32...ac) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_attr(x.ast, m, a2)).index);
    }
    for (int32:e2 in 0i32...ec) {
        drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, (raw item_extra(x.ast, m, e2)).index);
    }

    drop ast_scratch_set(x.ast, mark, 1i32, emitted);
    IdSpan:w = raw ast_scratch_commit(x.ast, mark);
    drop ast_set_decl_window(x.ast, mod_id, w.start, w.count);

    // The members are settled for this round; now their BODIES. Read back from the
    // node rather than from `m`, whose window is the one just replaced.
    DeclNode:m2 = raw ast_decl(x.ast, mod_id);
    int32:n2 = raw item_member_count(x.ast, m2);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...n2) {
        DeclId:id2 = raw item_member(x.ast, m2, j);
        DeclNode:d2 = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id2);
        if (d2.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) {
            discard(raw expand_module(x, id2));
        } else {
            discard(raw expand_in_decl(x, id2));
        }
    }
    pass true;
};

// --- where a splice landed --------------------------------------------------------
//
// WHAT A MACRO EMITS HAS TO FIT WHERE IT LANDED (`MACRO_REFERENCE.md` §2), and
// what "fit" means is different at each of the three sites. The site is passed IN
// rather than worked out from the body, because the body is the same in every case
// and only the surrounding declaration knows what it can hold.
//
//   MODULE   declarations, as written
//   STRUCT   variable declarations, CONVERTED to fields
//   IMPL     declarations, as written — the same for a `trait` body
//
// The struct case is the one that is not a copy. `int32:x;` parses as a STATEMENT
// inside a macro body and as a FIELD inside a struct, because those are different
// grammars reading the same text — so splicing one into the other is a conversion,
// which is exactly what §1's table says it is.
pub func:SITE_MODULE = int32() never fails { pass 1i32; };
pub func:SITE_STRUCT = int32() never fails { pass 2i32; };
pub func:SITE_IMPL = int32() never fails   { pass 3i32; };
pub func:SITE_ENUM = int32() never fails   { pass 4i32; };

func:site_name = string(int32:site) never fails {
    if (site == (raw SITE_MODULE())) { pass "at module level"; }
    if (site == (raw SITE_STRUCT())) { pass "in a struct body"; }
    if (site == (raw SITE_IMPL()))   { pass "in an impl or trait body"; }
    pass "in an enum body";
};

func:site_holds = string(int32:site) never fails {
    if (site == (raw SITE_STRUCT())) {
        pass "fields, so the body has to be variable declarations";
    }
    pass "declarations, so the body has to be declarations";
};

// A FIELD OUT OF A VARIABLE DECLARATION. A field holds a type, a name, its
// qualifiers and a `limit`, and all four travel (the last two since 1.0.8 and
// 1.5.8b step 6, below). An INITIALISER is what a field cannot hold, so it is
// refused rather than dropped: a `fixed int32:x = 5i32;` spliced as a field would
// silently lose the value.
func:splice_field = DeclId(Expander->:x, StmtId:src) never fails {
    StmtNode:v = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, src);

    // A NESTED INVOCATION PASSES THROUGH AS A SPLICE and expands on the next round,
    // which is what makes a struct-body macro able to invoke another one (`bug598`).
    if (v.kind == StmtKind.StmtExprStmt) {
        ExprId:ex = ExprId{ index: v.a };
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(ex))) {
            ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ex);
            if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
                ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, ex, raw CLONE_FUEL());
                pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice, v.span,
                                         c.index, 0i32, 0i32, 0i64));
            }
        }
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            "a struct body holds fields, and this line of the macro's body is an expression rather than a declaration",
            v.span);
        pass (raw decl_none());
    }

    if (v.kind != StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            "a struct body holds fields, and this line of the macro's body does not declare one",
            v.span);
        pass (raw decl_none());
    }
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw stmt_decl_init(x.ast, v)))) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            "a field has no initialiser, so this declaration cannot be spliced into a struct body with one written on it",
            v.span);
        pass (raw decl_none());
    }
    // THE QUALIFIER TRAVELS (1.0.8). A field DOES carry qualifiers — slot `c`,
    // read by `p_qualifiers` exactly as a statement declaration's is — and this
    // refused a `wild int8->:buf;` in a macro body with "a field carries no
    // qualifiers", blaming the language for what the splice dropped: it wrote
    // `0i32` into the slot. The same bits, copied across.
    // AND SO DOES THE `limit<Rules>` (D-308, 1.5.8b step 6): slot `b`, CLONED --
    // a verify node shared between two expansions is resolved once and the
    // last expansion wins (1.5.1's finding, `clone_verify`'s reason). A macro
    // that writes `limit<r> int64:n;` in a struct body gets a limited field,
    // where this splice wrote `0i32` and silently dropped the rule.
    // AND THE TYPE IS CLONED (DEF-189): `int32[N]:arr;` spliced as a field is
    // `int32[<the argument>]`, this instantiation's own.
    TypeId:fty = raw clone_type(x, raw stmt_decl_type(v), raw CLONE_FUEL());
    VerifyId:flim = raw clone_verify(x, raw stmt_decl_limit(x.ast, v), raw CLONE_FUEL());
    pass (raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, DeclKind.DeclFieldDecl, v.span,
                             fty.index, flim.index,
                             raw stmt_quals(x.ast, v), v.payload));
};

// AN ALIAS AT A DECLARATION SITE, PASSED THROUGH (DEF-171). The body's one
// invocation is cloned with the alias's arguments substituted and pushed as a
// splice of its own; the caller's window then holds it where the alias stood, and
// the round after expands it. It carries the span it was written at, in the
// alias's body, as a nested splice in a declaration body and a nested invocation
// among a struct macro's fields already do -- so a refusal of the target lands
// there, and the recorded site is what tells the reader which invocation of the
// alias brought it.
func:splice_alias = int32(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d, DeclNode:md, ExprNode:inv,
                          StmtNode:only) never fails {
    int32:saved_ps = x.params_start;
    int32:saved_pc = x.params_count;
    int32:saved_as = x.args_start;
    int32:saved_ac = x.args_count;
    int32:gcount = raw builtin_generic_count(inv);
    x.params_start = (raw macro_param_span(x.ast, md)).start;
    x.params_count = raw macro_param_count(x.ast, md);
    x.args_start = (raw expr_list_start(inv)) + gcount;
    x.args_count = (raw expr_list_count(inv)) - gcount;
    // A declaration site (D-340): the alias's arguments are module-level text.
    bool:saved_site = x.at_decl_site;
    int32:saved_md = x.mod_depth;
    x.at_decl_site = true;
    x.mod_depth = 0i32;

    drop record_site(x, md, d.span);
    int64:hmark = raw ast_built_mark(x.ast);
    ExprId:c = raw clone_expr(x, ExprId{ index: only.a }, raw CLONE_FUEL());

    x.params_start = saved_ps;
    x.params_count = saved_pc;
    x.args_start = saved_as;
    x.args_count = saved_ac;
    x.at_decl_site = saved_site;
    x.mod_depth = saved_md;

    // The clone is an invocation with its arguments: measured from itself, as the
    // declarations a splice emits are.
    if ((raw ast_depth_pass(x.ast, hmark)) != 0i32) {
        if (!x.blown) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
                "this expansion passes on an invocation whose arguments nest deeper than 256 levels (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
                d.span);
        }
        x.blown = true;
    }
    drop blank_tree(x, raw splice_invocation(d), raw CLONE_FUEL());
    if (raw expr_is_none(c)) { pass 0i32; }

    DeclId:s = raw ast_add_decl(x.ast, DeclKind.DeclMacroSplice, only.span,
                                  c.index, 0i32, 0i32, 0i64);
    drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, s.index);
    pass 1i32;
};

// ONE SPLICE, INSTANTIATED. Returns how many declarations it pushed, because the
// caller is building a window and has to know.
func:expand_splice = int32(Expander->:x, DeclNode:d, int32:site) never fails {
    ExprNode:inv = raw ast_expr(x.ast, raw splice_invocation(d));
    int32:name = raw builtin_name(inv);

    int32:decl = raw macrotable_find(@x.macros, name, x.cur_module);
    if (decl < 0i32) {
        // NOT FOUND HERE IS TWO DIFFERENT MISTAKES and they get two codes: a name
        // nobody declared, and a name declared in a module this one cannot reach.
        if (raw macrotable_find_elsewhere(@x.macros, name)) {
            string:l1 = string_concat("`#", raw intern_get(x.interns, name));
            string:l2 = string_concat(l1, "` is declared in another module, and a macro is invocable only in the module that declares it");
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_NOT_LOCAL(), move(l2), d.span);
            pass 0i32;
        }
        string:m1 = string_concat("`#", raw intern_get(x.interns, name));
        string:m2 = string_concat(m1, "` names no macro; `#` is also how a compiler builtin is spelled, so check the name against the macro's declaration");
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_UNKNOWN(), move(m2), d.span);
        pass 0i32;
    }
    // The probe asks only who is still standing, and this splice is.
    if (raw probe_standing(x, raw splice_invocation(d))) { pass 0i32; }

    DeclNode:md = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: decl });
    int32:pcount = raw macro_param_count(x.ast, md);
    int32:gcount = raw builtin_generic_count(inv);
    int32:acount = (raw expr_list_count(inv)) - gcount;

    if (acount != pcount) {
        string:n1 = string_concat("`#", raw intern_get(x.interns, name));
        string:n2 = string_concat(n1, "` takes ");
        string:n3 = string_concat(n2, int_to_string(pcount => int64));
        string:n4 = string_concat(n3, " argument(s) and this passes ");
        string:n5 = string_concat(n4, int_to_string(acount => int64));
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_ARITY(), move(n5), d.span);
        pass 0i32;
    }

    // AN ENUM BODY HOLDS VARIANTS, AND NO MACRO BODY SPELLS ONE. A variant is a
    // name with an optional payload and there is no standalone form of it a macro
    // body could contain — so this is the absence of a spelling rather than a
    // restriction, and inventing a mapping from some other body shape would be
    // inventing a rule.
    if (site == (raw SITE_ENUM())) {
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            "an enum body holds variants, and no macro body can contain one; a macro cannot emit enum variants",
            d.span);
        pass 0i32;
    }

    // A BODY THAT IS NOTHING BUT ONE INVOCATION IS WHATEVER ITS TARGET IS (D-125,
    // MACRO_REFERENCE §1; DEF-171, 1.6.1e step 3 -- the library listener's
    // mc0046b). The parse cannot know what `macro:alias = () { #b(); };` is, so
    // it reads an expression body; and at every declaration site the kind check
    // below then refused the alias for being one, whatever `b` was. The alias is
    // passed through instead: its one invocation becomes a splice standing where
    // the alias stood, the arguments substituted, and the next round expands THAT
    // as what its target is -- so a target that does not fit the site is refused
    // by the target's own check, once.
    //
    // NOT EVERY `#name(...)` IS AN INVOCATION. `#caller(name)` is consumed by the
    // clone and names a value, and a compiler builtin (`#size_of<T>()`) IS a
    // value: a body of either is known to be an expression, and the kind check
    // below is the right refusal for it. A name that is neither a macro of this
    // module nor a builtin is passed through, because what is wrong there is the
    // name, and the target's check is the one that says so.
    if ((raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, md)) == (raw MACRO_BODY_EXPR())) {
        StmtNode:only = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, StmtId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, 0i32) });
        if (only.kind == StmtKind.StmtExprStmt) {
            ExprNode:target = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ExprId{ index: only.a });
            if (target.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
                bool:is_alias = !(raw is_caller_form(x, target));
                if ((raw macro_here(x, target)) < 0i32) {
                    if (raw is_hash_builtin(raw intern_get(x.interns, raw builtin_name(target)))) {
                        is_alias = false;
                    }
                }
                if (is_alias) {
                    pass (raw splice_alias(x, d, md, inv, only));
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // WHAT THE SITE ACCEPTS. A struct body takes variable declarations and turns
    // them into fields; everywhere else takes declarations as written.
    int32:want = raw MACRO_BODY_DECLS();
    if (site == (raw SITE_STRUCT())) { want = raw MACRO_BODY_STMTS(); }

    if ((raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, md)) != want) {
        string:w1 = string_concat("this macro's body does not fit ",
                                        raw site_name(site));
        string:w2 = string_concat(w1, ", which holds ");
        string:w3 = string_concat(w2, raw site_holds(site));
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(), move(w3), d.span);
        pass 0i32;
    }

    int32:saved_ps = x.params_start;
    int32:saved_pc = x.params_count;
    int32:saved_as = x.args_start;
    int32:saved_ac = x.args_count;

    // The parameter names and the argument expressions both live in windows, and
    // binding is positional.
    x.params_start = (raw macro_param_span(x.ast, md)).start;
    x.params_count = pcount;
    x.args_start = (raw expr_list_start(inv)) + gcount;
    x.args_count = acount;
    // A DECLARATION SITE (D-340): this invocation stands at module level, in a
    // struct's body or in an `impl`'s, where the only scope is the module's. Its
    // arguments resolve THERE -- not inside the declarations the body emits,
    // where a parameter or a local of the emitted function captured them
    // (`macro:mk = (V) { func:f = int32(int32:a) { pass a + V; }; };` over
    // `#mk(a)` answered 10 for 105).
    bool:saved_site = x.at_decl_site;
    int32:saved_md = x.mod_depth;
    x.at_decl_site = true;
    x.mod_depth = 0i32;

    drop record_site(x, md, d.span);

    int64:hmark = raw ast_built_mark(x.ast);
    int32:bcount = raw macro_body_count(x.ast, md);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...bcount) {
        if (site == (raw SITE_STRUCT())) {
            DeclId:f = raw splice_field(x, StmtId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, i) });
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, f.index);
        } else {
            DeclId:src = DeclId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, md, i) };
            DeclId:c = raw clone_decl(x, src, raw CLONE_FUEL());
            drop ast_scratch_push(x.ast, c.index);
        }
    }
    // A declaration lands at the module's level: each root it carries is measured
    // from itself, so the question is whether any cloned node is too tall.
    if ((raw ast_depth_pass(x.ast, hmark)) != 0i32) {
        if (!x.blown) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_TOO_DEEP(),
                "this expansion emits a declaration that nests deeper than 256 levels (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)",
                d.span);
        }
        x.blown = true;
    }

    x.params_start = saved_ps;
    x.params_count = saved_pc;
    x.args_start = saved_as;
    x.args_count = saved_ac;
    x.at_decl_site = saved_site;
    x.mod_depth = saved_md;

    // The splice's own invocation is detached now — its arguments were cloned into
    // the body — so it is blanked rather than left for the audit to find and refuse.
    drop blank_tree(x, raw splice_invocation(d), raw CLONE_FUEL());
    pass bcount;
};

pub func:expander_blown = bool(Expander->:x) never fails { pass x.blown; };

// --- what is decided at the declarations (DEF-172, DEF-173; 1.6.1e step 3) ---------
//
// A MACRO THAT INVOKES ITSELF, DIRECTLY OR THROUGH OTHERS, NEVER SETTLES, and the
// declarations say so before one round has run. A body has no conditional: what it
// invokes, it invokes at every instantiation, so a cycle among the invocations the
// bodies write is non-termination the moment a member is invoked -- and
// MACRO_REFERENCE §7's own example, `macro:m = () { #m(); };  // refused`,
// invokes nothing. Until this existed that declaration was ACCEPTED (the library
// listener's mc0246), and an invoked cycle ran the rounds to their bound and was
// reported at module 0's root -- `prelude.npk:17:1`, a file the reader did not
// write -- in a sentence naming neither macro (mc0251).
//
// THE EDGES ARE READ OFF THE BODY'S EXPRESSION RANGE, which the parser records on
// the declaration: every `#name(...)` written between the braces, wherever it
// stands, that names a macro of the SAME module. A macro is invocable only where
// it is declared (D-124), so another module's macro of that name is no edge, and
// two modules' macros cannot form a cycle.
//
// REPORTED ONCE PER CYCLE, AT ITS FIRST MACRO IN SOURCE ORDER: a macro is refused
// when a chain of invocations leads from it back to it through macros declared
// AT OR AFTER it, and the shortest such chain is the one the sentence names. So
// `ping` -> `pong` -> `ping` is one report, at `ping`; `pong` is not the first of
// any cycle and is not reported again.
//
// AND WHAT THE RULE COSTS: an invocation written as an ARGUMENT to a macro whose
// body never mentions that parameter is dropped by the expansion, so a cycle
// through one would settle -- and is refused here all the same. The edge is what
// the body writes, not what an instantiation happens to keep.

// WHICH ENTRY A NAME IS in module `owner` -- its place in the table, where
// `macrotable_find` answers the declaration -- or -1.
func:macrotable_index = int32(MacroTable->:t, int32:name, int32:owner) never fails {
    int64:i = 0i64;
    while (i < t.v.count) decreases t.v.count - i {
        MacroEntry:e = t.v[i];
        if (e.name == name) {
            if (e.owner == owner) { pass (i =>! int32); }
        }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

// A `macro:` DECLARED INSIDE A MACRO BODY IS REFUSED WHERE IT IS WRITTEN. Macros
// are collected once, before the first round, from the modules' own members; one
// that an expansion emitted would enter no table and could never be invoked. The
// clone has no case for the kind, so until this step the outer macro's first
// instantiation reported "this declaration kind has no entry in the macro clone"
// -- MACRO-006, a defect of the compiler by its own sentence, about a program that
// was simply wrong. The descent is the clone's: the members of the items a body
// declares, and of an `impl`.
func:refuse_nested_macros = NIL(Expander->:x, DeclId:id, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw decl_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(x.ast, id);
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclMacroDecl) {
        string:m1 = string_concat("macro `", raw intern_get(x.interns, raw decl_name(d)));
        drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_WRONG_SHAPE(),
            string_concat(m1, "` is declared inside a macro body, and a body cannot emit one: macros are collected before expansion begins, so a `macro:` that an expansion produced could never be invoked; declare it beside the macro that needs it"),
            d.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    bool:is_item = (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclStructDecl);
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumDecl)   { is_item = true; }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl)  { is_item = true; }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl) { is_item = true; }
    if (is_item) {
        int32:mc = raw item_member_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:m in 0i32...mc) {
            drop refuse_nested_macros(x, raw item_member(x.ast, d, m), fuel - 1i32);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (d.kind == DeclKind.DeclImplDecl) {
        int32:ic = raw impl_member_count(x.ast, d);
        for (int32:im in 0i32...ic) {
            drop refuse_nested_macros(x, raw impl_member(x.ast, d, im), fuel - 1i32);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- what a body may not write about its own parameters (DEF-189) -------------------
//
// AN ARGUMENT IS AN EXPRESSION (MACRO_REFERENCE §3), so there are two things a body
// cannot do with a parameter's name -- and each was accepted in silence:
//
//   * USE IT AS A TYPE'S NAME. `macro:mk = (T) { T:x = T{ v: 7i32 }; … };` beside a
//     module `struct:T` built the module's `T` whatever was passed: the argument
//     dropped, exit 7 for `#mk(3i32)`. A named type, a struct literal's name and the
//     type a destructuring pattern names are NAMES, not expressions; no argument can
//     be substituted there. (A compile-time VALUE in an argument list is the one
//     place the two look alike: `simd<int32, N>` reads `N` as a type's name, by
//     the parser's rule that a bare identifier in that list is one, and
//     `simd<int32, (N)>` reads it as the expression it is.)
//   * DECLARE IT AND USE IT. `macro:bump = (N) { int32:N = 1i32; … N + 1i32 … };`
//     declared a local `N` and read the ARGUMENT at every `N` after it -- exit 41
//     for `#bump(40i32)`: a declaration's name is not an identifier expression and
//     is never replaced, and every use of it is. A local, a `for` binding, a
//     pattern's binding, a function's parameter and a declaration the body emits
//     each do this.
//
// A NAME THE BODY DECLARES AND NEVER WRITES AS AN EXPRESSION IS LEFT ALONE. It is
// MACRO_REFERENCE §10's open question -- "may a parameter name an emitted
// declaration?": `macro:m = (N) { func:N = …; };` emits a function literally
// called `N`, "unimplemented rather than refused" -- and refusing it would be
// settling that question here (S-123, the user's). What IS refused is the half of
// it that answers wrongly: the same body calling `N()` would call the ARGUMENT.
// A field and a variant are reached through `.`, are no identifier, and are no
// declaration in this sense at all.
//
// READ OFF THE BODY'S ID RANGES, which the parser records on the declaration, for
// the reason the cycle check reads the expression range: every node written
// between the braces is in them, wherever it stands. ONE REPORT PER PARAMETER PER
// MACRO, at its first such spelling in source order.
struct:ParamUse = {
    bool:names_type;    // written where a type's name stands
    Span:type_at;       // the first such spelling
    bool:declared;      // declared by the body
    Span:decl_at;       // the first such declaration
    bool:used;          // written as an identifier expression (and not as `#caller`'s name)
};

// Which parameter of `md` a name is, or -1.
func:macro_param_of = int32(Expander->:x, DeclNode:md, int32:name) never fails {
    int32:pc = raw macro_param_count(x.ast, md);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...pc) {
        if ((raw macro_param(x.ast, md, i)) == name) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

func:note_param_type = NIL(Expander->:x, List<ParamUse>->:uses, DeclNode:md, int32:name,
                           Span:at) never fails {
    int32:i = raw macro_param_of(x, md, name);
    if (i < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ParamUse:u = (<-uses)[i => int64];
    bool:take = !u.names_type;
    if (!take) { take = raw span_before(at, u.type_at); }
    if (take) { u.names_type = true; u.type_at = at; (<-uses)[i => int64] = u; }
    pass NIL;
};

func:note_param_decl = NIL(Expander->:x, List<ParamUse>->:uses, DeclNode:md, int32:name,
                           Span:at) never fails {
    int32:i = raw macro_param_of(x, md, name);
    if (i < 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ParamUse:u = (<-uses)[i => int64];
    bool:take = !u.declared;
    if (!take) { take = raw span_before(at, u.decl_at); }
    if (take) { u.declared = true; u.decl_at = at; (<-uses)[i => int64] = u; }
    pass NIL;
};

func:check_macro_params = NIL(Expander->:x, DeclNode:md, List<ParamUse>->:uses,
                              List<int32>->:escaped) never fails {
    int32:pc = raw macro_param_count(x.ast, md);
    if (pc == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop list_clear(uses);
    drop list_clear(escaped);
    for (int32:z in 0i32...pc) {
        drop list_push(uses, ParamUse{ names_type: false, type_at: md.span,
                                       declared: false, decl_at: md.span, used: false });
    }

    // A named type whose name is a parameter. A builtin type keyword's payload is
    // its token kind, not a name.
    int32:ti = raw macro_body_type_lo(x.ast, md);
    int32:thi = raw macro_body_type_hi(x.ast, md);
    while (ti < thi) decreases thi - ti {
        TypeNode:tn = raw ast_type(x.ast, TypeId{ index: ti });
        if (tn.kind == TypeKind.TypeNamedType) {
            if (!(raw type_name_is_builtin(tn))) {
                drop note_param_type(x, uses, md, (raw type_name_index(tn)) =>! int32, tn.span);
            }
        }
        ti = ti + 1i32;
    }

    // The expressions: a struct literal's name is a type's; and the name written
    // in `#caller(name)` is copied by NAME, never substituted, so it is no use.
    int32:elo = raw macro_body_expr_lo(x.ast, md);
    int32:ehi = raw macro_body_expr_hi(x.ast, md);
    int32:ei = elo;
    while (ei < ehi) decreases ehi - ei {
        ExprNode:en = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ExprId{ index: ei });
        if (en.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
            drop note_param_type(x, uses, md, (raw expr_name(en)) =>! int32, en.span);
        }
        if (raw is_caller_form(x, en)) {
            if ((raw expr_list_count(en)) == 1i32) {
                drop list_push(escaped, raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw expr_list_start(en), 0i32));
            }
        }
        ei = ei + 1i32;
    }
    // A USE: an identifier expression spelling the parameter -- exactly the node
    // `clone_expr` replaces with the argument.
    ei = elo;
    while (ei < ehi) decreases ehi - ei {
        ExprNode:un = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ExprId{ index: ei });
        if (un.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            int32:upi = raw macro_param_of(x, md, (raw expr_name(un)) =>! int32);
            if (upi >= 0i32) {
                bool:is_escape = false;
                int64:ek = 0i64;
                while (ek < (<-escaped).count) decreases (<-escaped).count - ek {
                    if ((<-escaped)[ek] == ei) { is_escape = true; }
                    ek = ek + 1i64;
                }
                if (!is_escape) {
                    ParamUse:uu = (<-uses)[upi => int64];
                    uu.used = true;
                    (<-uses)[upi => int64] = uu;
                }
            }
        }
        ei = ei + 1i32;
    }

    // A destructuring pattern: the enum it names (every segment but the last,
    // which is the variant) and the names it binds. A struct pattern's type is a
    // type node and was read above.
    int32:pi = raw macro_body_pat_lo(x.ast, md);
    int32:phi = raw macro_body_pat_hi(x.ast, md);
    while (pi < phi) decreases phi - pi {
        PatNode:pn = raw ast_pat(x.ast, PatId{ index: pi });
        if (pn.kind == PatKind.PatEnumDestructure) {
            int32:segs = raw pat_enum_segment_count(x.ast, pn);
            for (int32:sg in 0i32...(segs - 1i32)) {
                drop note_param_type(x, uses, md, raw pat_enum_segment(x.ast, pn, sg), pn.span);
            }
            int32:ebc = raw pat_enum_bind_count(x.ast, pn);
            for (int32:eb in 0i32...ebc) {
                drop note_param_decl(x, uses, md, raw pat_enum_bind(x.ast, pn, eb), pn.span);
            }
        }
        if (pn.kind == PatKind.PatStructDestructure) {
            int32:sbc = raw pat_bind_count(pn);
            for (int32:sb in 0i32...sbc) {
                drop note_param_decl(x, uses, md, raw ast_id_at(x.ast, raw pat_bind_start(pn), sb),
                                     pn.span);
            }
        }
        pi = pi + 1i32;
    }

    // A local.
    int32:si = raw macro_body_stmt_lo(x.ast, md);
    int32:shi = raw macro_body_stmt_hi(x.ast, md);
    while (si < shi) decreases shi - si {
        StmtNode:sn = raw ast_stmt(x.ast, StmtId{ index: si });
        if (sn.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
            drop note_param_decl(x, uses, md, raw stmt_name(sn), sn.span);
        }
        si = si + 1i32;
    }

    // A declaration whose name an identifier can mean: a parameter (a function's,
    // a `for` binding), a variadic tail, a generic parameter, and what the body
    // emits. NOT a field, a variant or an attribute -- none is an identifier.
    int32:di = raw macro_body_decl_lo(x.ast, md);
    int32:dhi = raw macro_body_decl_hi(x.ast, md);
    while (di < dhi) decreases dhi - di {
        DeclNode:dn = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: di });
        bool:names = (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclParamDecl);
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclVariadicSpec)  { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclGenericParam)  { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl)  { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclGlobalDecl)    { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclStructDecl)    { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclEnumDecl)      { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclTraitDecl)     { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclRuleDecl)      { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclUnitDecl)      { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclErrorDecl)     { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclModuleDecl)    { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclAssocTypeDecl) { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclOpaqueDecl)    { names = true; }
        if (dn.kind == DeclKind.DeclExternFn)      { names = true; }
        if (names) {
            drop note_param_decl(x, uses, md, raw decl_name(dn), dn.span);
        }
        di = di + 1i32;
    }

    string:mname = raw intern_get(x.interns, raw decl_name(md));
    for (int32:r in 0i32...pc) {
        ParamUse:u = (<-uses)[r => int64];
        // The two violations, and the earlier of them where a parameter has both.
        bool:bad_type = u.names_type;
        bool:bad_decl = (u.declared && u.used);
        if ((!bad_type) && (!bad_decl)) { continue; }
        if (bad_type && bad_decl) {
            if (raw span_before(u.decl_at, u.type_at)) { bad_type = false; } else { bad_decl = false; }
        }
        string:pname = raw intern_get(x.interns, raw macro_param(x.ast, md, r));
        string:m1 = string_concat("`", pname);
        string:m2 = string_concat(m1, "` is a parameter of macro `");
        string:m3 = string_concat(m2, mname);
        if (bad_type) {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_PARAM_FORM(),
                string_concat(m3, "`, and here it stands where a type's name stands: an argument is an expression and cannot name a type, so nothing would be substituted and this would mean whatever the name means where the macro is written. Rename the parameter or the type; where a compile-time VALUE is meant in an argument list, write the parameter in parentheses -- `simd<int32, (N)>` (MACRO_REFERENCE §3)"),
                u.type_at);
        } else {
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_PARAM_FORM(),
                string_concat(m3, "`, and the body both declares that name here and writes it as an expression: a declaration's name is never substituted and every use of the name is, so each use would be the argument and not this declaration. Rename one of them (MACRO_REFERENCE §3)"),
                u.decl_at);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE INVOCATION GRAPH AND ONE SEARCH'S WORKING LISTS, in one place so the search
// is handed one pointer.
struct:MacroGraph = {
    List<int32>:adj_lo;   // entry `m` invokes adj[adj_lo[m] .. adj_lo[m + 1])
    List<int32>:adj;
    List<int32>:seen;     // the search that last reached an entry, as `s + 1`
    List<int32>:par;      // the entry it was reached from
    List<int32>:queue;
    List<int32>:chain;
};

// THE SHORTEST CHAIN FROM ENTRY `s` BACK TO ITSELF through entries at or after it,
// breadth first. On `true` the chain is left in `g.chain`, LAST LINK FIRST: the
// entry that invokes `s`, then the one that invokes that, back to `s` itself.
// `seen` is stamped rather than cleared, so one list serves every search.
func:macro_cycle_from = bool(MacroGraph->:g, int32:s, int64:n) never fails {
    int32:stamp = s + 1i32;
    drop list_clear(@g.queue);
    drop list_push(@g.queue, s);
    g.seen[s => int64] = stamp;
    g.par[s => int64] = 0i32 - 1i32;
    int64:head = 0i64;
    // Each entry is queued at most once (`seen`), so the queue never holds more
    // than the `n` entries and `n - head` falls with every one taken off it.
    while (head < g.queue.count) decreases n - head {
        int32:v = g.queue[head];
        head = head + 1i64;
        int32:e = g.adj_lo[v => int64];
        int32:e_end = g.adj_lo[(v => int64) + 1i64];
        while (e < e_end) decreases e_end - e {
            int32:w = g.adj[e => int64];
            if (w == s) {
                drop list_clear(@g.chain);
                int32:back = v;
                // `par` leads from `v` to `s` over entries this search queued,
                // each once: no further than the queue is long.
                int64:left = g.queue.count;
                while (back >= 0i32) decreases left {
                    drop list_push(@g.chain, back);
                    back = g.par[back => int64];
                    left = left - 1i64;
                }
                pass true;
            }
            if (w > s) {
                if (g.seen[w => int64] != stamp) {
                    g.seen[w => int64] = stamp;
                    g.par[w => int64] = v;
                    drop list_push(@g.queue, w);
                }
            }
            e = e + 1i32;
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// RUN BY THE DRIVER AFTER COLLECTION AND BEFORE THE FIRST ROUND; it does not
// expand a program this refuses.
pub func:check_macro_decls = NIL(Expander->:x) never fails {
    int64:n = x.macros.v.count;
    if (n == 0i64) { pass NIL; }

    // The nested declarations first: a body that declares a macro is refused for
    // that, whatever it invokes.
    int64:k = 0i64;
    while (k < n) decreases n - k {
        DeclNode:kd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: (x.macros.v[k]).decl });
        if ((raw macro_body_kind(x.ast, kd)) == (raw MACRO_BODY_DECLS())) {
            int32:bc = raw macro_body_count(x.ast, kd);
            for (int32:b in 0i32...bc) {
                drop refuse_nested_macros(x, DeclId{ index: raw macro_body_at(x.ast, kd, b) },
                                          raw CLONE_FUEL());
            }
        }
        k = k + 1i64;
    }

    // Then what each body writes about its own parameters.
    List<ParamUse>:uses = raw list_init::<ParamUse>(8i64);
    List<int32>:escaped = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
    int64:q = 0i64;
    while (q < n) decreases n - q {
        DeclNode:qd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: (x.macros.v[q]).decl });
        drop check_macro_params(x, qd, @uses, @escaped);
        q = q + 1i64;
    }

    MacroGraph:g = MacroGraph{
        adj_lo: raw list_init::<int32>(n + 1i64),
        adj:    raw list_init::<int32>(16i64),
        seen:   raw list_init::<int32>(n),
        par:    raw list_init::<int32>(n),
        queue:  raw list_init::<int32>(n),
        chain:  raw list_init::<int32>(8i64)
    };

    // The edges, entry by entry.
    int64:m = 0i64;
    while (m < n) decreases n - m {
        MacroEntry:me = x.macros.v[m];
        DeclNode:md = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: me.decl });
        drop list_push(@g.adj_lo, g.adj.count =>! int32);
        drop list_push(@g.seen, 0i32);
        drop list_push(@g.par, 0i32 - 1i32);
        int32:ei = raw macro_body_expr_lo(x.ast, md);
        int32:ehi = raw macro_body_expr_hi(x.ast, md);
        while (ei < ehi) decreases ehi - ei {
            ExprNode:en = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ExprId{ index: ei });
            // `#caller(name)` in a body is the hygiene escape, consumed by the
            // clone by its NAME: it is never an invocation, whatever is declared.
            if ((en.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) && !(raw is_caller_form(x, en))) {
                int32:t = raw macrotable_index(@x.macros, raw builtin_name(en), me.owner);
                if (t >= 0i32) { drop list_push(@g.adj, t); }
            }
            ei = ei + 1i32;
        }
        m = m + 1i64;
    }
    drop list_push(@g.adj_lo, g.adj.count =>! int32);

    int64:s = 0i64;
    while (s < n) decreases n - s {
        if (raw macro_cycle_from(@g, s =>! int32, n)) {
            // `g.chain` holds the cycle's entries last link first, ending at `s`.
            string:nm = raw intern_get(x.interns, (x.macros.v[s]).name);
            string:msg = string_concat("macro `", nm);
            msg = string_concat(msg, "` never settles: `");
            msg = string_concat(msg, nm);
            if (g.chain.count == 1i64) {
                msg = string_concat(msg, "` invokes itself");
            } else {
                msg = string_concat(msg, "` invokes `");
                // From the entry `s` invokes to the one that invokes `s`: the
                // chain read backwards, its last element (`s` itself) left out.
                int64:c = g.chain.count - 2i64;
                while (c >= 0i64) decreases c {
                    msg = string_concat(msg, raw intern_get(x.interns,
                                    (x.macros.v[g.chain[c] => int64]).name));
                    msg = string_concat(msg, "`, which invokes `");
                    c = c - 1i64;
                }
                msg = string_concat(msg, nm);
                msg = string_concat(msg, "`");
            }
            msg = string_concat(msg, " (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)");
            DeclNode:sd = raw ast_decl(x.ast, DeclId{ index: (x.macros.v[s]).decl });
            drop expand_err(x, raw MACRO_NO_FIXPOINT(), move(msg), sd.span);
        }
        s = s + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the round bound, and who is standing at it (DEF-173) ---------------------------
//
// WITH THE CYCLES REFUSED AT THE DECLARATIONS, WHAT REACHES THE BOUND IS A CHAIN
// THAT IS FINITE AND TOO LONG: each round expands one level, and the driver stops
// after `EXPAND_ROUNDS`. It then takes ONE MORE WALK THAT INSTANTIATES NOTHING --
// the probe -- in which every place that would instantiate records the invocation
// it met instead. The first one met is where the refusal points, and its macro is
// the one the sentence names; if the walk meets none, the last round was the last
// one needed and the program has settled.
//
// A WALK, NOT A SCAN OF THE ARRAY, because "is this an invocation of a macro" is
// asked per module (D-124) and the array cannot say which module a node is in.

// Is the walk probing? If so the invocation is recorded -- the first one only --
// and the caller instantiates nothing.
func:probe_standing = bool(Expander->:x, ExprId:inv) never fails {
    if (!x.probing) { pass false; }
    if (x.standing == 0i32) { x.standing = inv.index; }
    pass true;
};

pub func:expand_probe_begin = NIL(Expander->:x) never fails {
    x.probing = true;
    x.standing = 0i32;
    pass NIL;
};

// THE ROUNDS DID NOT SETTLE: reported at the invocation the probe found standing,
// which is in the program -- never at a module's root, which for module 0 is the
// prelude's first line. Nothing is reported when nothing stands.
pub func:expand_no_fixpoint = NIL(Expander->:x) never fails {
    x.probing = false;
    if (x.standing == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:inv = raw ast_expr(x.ast, ExprId{ index: x.standing });
    string:m1 = string_concat("macro expansion did not settle within its ",
                                    int_to_string((raw EXPAND_ROUNDS()) => int64));
    string:m2 = string_concat(m1, " rounds: `#");
    string:m3 = string_concat(m2, raw intern_get(x.interns, raw builtin_name(inv)));
    drop diaglist_push(x.diags, raw diag_error(raw MACRO_NO_FIXPOINT(),
        string_concat(m3, "` is still standing here after the last of them. A chain of macros each invoking the next is followed one level a round and no further than that; a macro that reaches itself is refused at its declaration, so this chain is finite and too long -- shorten it (MACRO_REFERENCE §7)"),
        inv.span));
    pass NIL;
};
